00m in a world record time of 47.6 seconds.","ok":true}],"note":"47,60 s (47,6) sat 6. oktober 1985 i Canberra; rekorden står stadig."},"rec|Hvor hurtigt løb Usain Bolt 100 m i 2009 (mænds verdensrekord)?":{"pool":"rec","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/fastest-run-100-metres-(male)","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"On 16 August 2009, Usain Bolt (Jamaica) won the 100 m final of the World Athletics Championships in Berlin, Germany, in a time of 9.58 seconds.","ok":true},{"u":"https://worldathletics.org/news/news/bolt-again-958-world-record-in-berlin-updat","d":"worldathletics.org","q":"Usain Bolt set a new 100m World record of 9.58","ok":true}],"note":"9,58 s sat 16. august 2009 ved VM i Berlin; rekorden står stadig."},"rec|Hvor hurtigt løb Usain Bolt 200 m i 2009 (mænds verdensrekord)?":{"pool":"rec","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/fastest-run-200-metres-(male)","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"Bolt won the 200 metres at the IAAF World Championships with this run","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usain_Bolt","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"This was recorded at the 2009 World Championships in Athletics in Berlin","ok":true}],"note":"19,19 s sat 20. august 2009 ved VM i Berlin; rekorden står stadig."},"who|Eiffeltårnet":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","fixed":true,"date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffeltårnet","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Tårnet er 330 meter højt inklusive tårnets antennekonstruktion.","ok":true},{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffeltårnet","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Eiffeltårnet blev bygget til Verdensudstillingen i 1889","ok":true},{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffeltårnet","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"ved at samle 18.038 stykker smedejern med 2,5 millioner nitter","ok":true},{"u":"https://theconversation.com/the-eiffel-tower-gets-bigger-every-summer-heres-why-261904","d":"theconversation.com","q":"the Eiffel Tower grows even taller than its original design","ok":true},{"u":"https://theconversation.com/the-eiffel-tower-gets-bigger-every-summer-heres-why-261904","d":"theconversation.com","q":"Eiffel chose puddled iron for its construction","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/eiffel-tower-grows-summer-shrinks-winter/","d":"snopes.com","q":"The Eiffel Tower does grow and contract in the summer and winter, respectively, due to temperature fluctuations","ok":true}],"note":"Påstanden om 'op til ca. 15 cm højere' er omstridt: Eiffeltårnets egen side siger kun få millimeter (de 15 cm er tårnets sidelæns udsving i sol), mens andre kilder siger ","rechecked":"2026-11-13"},"who|Honningbi":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","fixed":true,"date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/bees/buzz.html","d":"pbs.org","q":"Bees possess five eyes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/bees/buzz.html","d":"pbs.org","q":"The bee leaves the stinger and venom pouch behind and soon dies due to abdominal rupture.","ok":true},{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honningbi","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Bierne har et meget kompliceret dansesprog, som de bruger, når de skal meddele hinanden hvor der er fundet god nektar","ok":true},{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honningbi","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"dels er den eneste bi i hele boet der forsyner familien med afkom","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"when properly stored, honey therefore does not spoil","ok":true}],"note":"Spor 5 er upræcist: arbejderbier dør normalt kun, når de stikker et pattedyr (hos andre insekter trækkes brodden ud), og dronningen overlever. Rettet til 'som regel ... e"},"who|Blæksprutte":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/article/octopus-anatomy-cephalopod-disguise-evolution","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"For starters, they have three hearts and blue blood.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/article/octopus-anatomy-cephalopod-disguise-evolution","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They have no bones.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/article/octopus-anatomy-cephalopod-disguise-evolution","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"they squirt a cloud of ink and jet off in another direction","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbcearth.com/factfiles/animals/molluscs/octopus","d":"bbcearth.com","q":"squeezing into any space larger than their beak","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbcearth.com/factfiles/animals/molluscs/octopus","d":"bbcearth.com","q":"the eight-armed cephalopods tend to use all of their limbs","ok":true}],"note":"Tre hjerter, blåt blod, otte arme, ingen knogler, blæk og evne til at presse sig gennem sprækker er alle bekræftet for ottearmede blæksprutter (octopus)."},"who|Månen":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","fixed":true,"date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/moon/weather-on-the-moon/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"The Moon has hardly any atmosphere and no global magnetic field to shield it from space radiation.","ok":true},{"u":"https://eos.org/features/seeing-the-light","d":"eos.org","q":"accurate measurement of how quickly the Moon is moving away from Earth: 3.8 centimeters per year.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/moon/moon-walkers/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"were the first of 12 human beings to walk on the Moon","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.space.com/20057-moon-phases-stargazing-facts.html","d":"space.com","q":"or 14.76 days from new moon), the moon has gone through half a synodic month.","ok":true}],"note":"Spor 2 'ingen atmosfære' er upræcist: Månen har en ekstremt tynd exosfære, så det rettes til 'næsten ingen atmosfære'. 3,8 cm/år, tolv på Månen og ca. 14,8 dage fra nymån"},"who|Vombat":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/common-wombat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"faces her rear rather than her head to prevent it filling with dirt when the mother is digging","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/common-wombat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Wombats use their strong claws to dig large burrows.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/common-wombat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"they are the only animal known to have cube-shaped dung","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.csiro.au/en/news/All/Articles/2022/July/10-things-about-wombats","d":"","q":"In wombats, the pouch faces backwards.","ok":false},{"u":"https://www.csiro.au/en/news/All/Articles/2022/July/10-things-about-wombats","d":"","q":"Wombats tunnel underground, digging holes big enough for a person to fall into.","ok":false},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/52640-wombats.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Wombats are small marsupials that look like a cross between a bear, a pig and a gopher","ok":true}],"note":"Australien, bagudvendt pung, store huler, kubeformet afføring og bamselignende udseende er bekræftet."},"who|Chokolade":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-39067088","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Chocolate is made from cocoa beans, which have been grown and consumed in the Americas for thousands of years.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-39067088","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"The Maya and the Aztecs made a drink out of cocoa beans called xocolatl","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Chocolate in Mesoamerica was a bitter drink","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the theobromine found in chocolate is toxic to animals such as cats, dogs, horses, parrots","ok":true},{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/history/article/the-secret-history-of-chocolate","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"mixing the seeds with chilies to make a spicy, frothy beverage","ok":true},{"u":"https://asbe.org/article/chocolate/","d":"asbe.org","q":"melts rapidly in the mouth at 98.5°F (37°C)","ok":true}],"note":"Kakaobønner fra kakaotræet, bitter/krydret aztekisk drik, smelter omkring kropstemperatur (ca. 37 °C) og er giftig for hunde (theobromin) er bekræftet."},"who|Rødvin":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.diffordsguide.com/beer-wine-spirits/category/641/wine-red","d":"diffordsguide.com","q":"The red colour of the wine comes from anthocyan pigments which are in the skin of the grape.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.diffordsguide.com/beer-wine-spirits/category/641/wine-red","d":"diffordsguide.com","q":"A small exchange of gasses through the pores of the oak supplies oxygen which softens the young wine","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.decanter.com/learn/wset/letting-the-wine-stew-maceration-factors-that-influence-wine-wset-level-2-282923/","d":"decanter.com","q":"come from the skin of the grape","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.decanter.com/learn/advice/let-wine-breathe-ask-decanter-363531/","d":"decanter.com","q":"Young, robust red wines benefit most from breathing, while delicate or older wines should be treated with care.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.davywine.co.uk/winemaking-techniques/","d":"davywine.co.uk","q":"Oak barrels bring character to a wine.","ok":true}],"note":"Rødvin laves af druer, farven kommer fra skallerne, den lagres ofte på egetræsfade, og unge rødvine drager fordel af at 'ånde' (karaffel)."},"who|Pizza":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/history/history-magazine/article/pizza-margherita-may-be-fit-for-a-queen-but-was-it-named-after-one","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The Margherita pizza is an iconic Neapolitan dish with tomatoes, mozzarella, and basil","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/history/history-magazine/article/pizza-margherita-may-be-fit-for-a-queen-but-was-it-named-after-one","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The iconic Neapolitan dish was allegedly named for an Italian queen after she sampled it in Naples","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20200415-how-to-make-pizza-like-a-neapolitan-master","d":"bbc.com","q":"the Margherita, topped with tomato sauce, mozzarella cheese and fresh basil","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.italymagazine.com/recipe/theres-something-about-pizza-margherita-heres-official-recipe","d":"italymagazine.com","q":"Queen Margherita of Savoy, wife of King Umberto I, visited Naples.","ok":true}],"note":"Pizza er napolitansk, Margherita er ifølge legenden opkaldt efter dronning Margherita (1889), og tomat/mozzarella er klassisk topping. Spor 3 er formuleret som 'ifølge le"},"who|Pingvin":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","fixed":true,"date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/blog/penguin-fact-sheet/","d":"pbs.org","q":"live almost exclusively in the Southern Hemisphere","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/blog/penguin-fact-sheet/","d":"pbs.org","q":"Their bodies are adapted for swimming and diving in the water","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With the exception of the emperor penguin, where the male does it all, all penguins share the incubation duties.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.whoi.edu/oceanus/feature/fascinating-facts-about-emperor-penguins/","d":"whoi.edu","q":"Male emperors keep the eggs warm, carefully cradling them on top of their feet","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.discoverwildlife.com/animal-facts/birds/facts-about-penguins","d":"discoverwildlife.com","q":"Penguins do have knees","ok":true}],"note":"Spor 3 'lever på den sydlige halvkugle' er upræcist, da Galápagospingvinen lever ved og lige nord for ækvator; rettet til 'næsten udelukkende'. Øvrige spor er korrekte."},"who|Regnbue":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://weather.metoffice.gov.uk/learn-about/weather/optical-effects/rainbows","d":"weather.metoffice.gov.uk","q":"rainbows are actually full circles","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zxh9cmn","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"you may be lucky and catch sight of a rainbow!","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zxh9cmn","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"The seven main colours we see are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.metlink.org/fieldwork-resource/rainbows/","d":"metlink.org","q":"Why can we never reach the end of the rainbow and find the pot of gold?","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.usgs.gov/water-science-school/science/rainbows-water-and-light","d":"usgs.gov","q":"thus come from light, sunlight in the rainbow","ok":true}],"note":"Lys, sol og regn samtidig, egentlig en cirkel (ses som bue fra jorden), syv klassiske farver og myten om guldskatten i enden er korrekte."},"who|Kamel":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Camelus_dromedarius/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"capable of drinking 100 L of water in just 10 minutes","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/27503-camels.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"They can drink 30 gallons (113 liters) of water in just 13 minutes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/27503-camels.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Two rows of long lashes also protect their eyes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/how-do-camels-survive-in-deserts.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"But they don't store water in them. Instead, their humps are made of fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/camel","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"The dromedary camel has one hump and the Bactrian camel has two.","ok":true}],"note":"Ørken, over 100 liter (ca. 113 liter på 13 minutter), puklen er fedt, to rækker øjenvipper og dromedar/baktrisk kamel (én/to pukler) er bekræftet."},"who|Titanic":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_the_Titanic","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"and was the largest ship in the world.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_the_Titanic","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"RMS Titanic sank in the North Atlantic Ocean on 15 April 1912.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.noaa.gov/office-of-general-counsel/gc-international-section/rms-titanic-history-and-significance","d":"","q":"set sail on its maiden voyage from Southampton on April 10, 1912","ok":false},{"u":"https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/maritime-history/rms-titanic-facts","d":"rmg.co.uk","q":"hit an iceberg in the North Atlantic Ocean during its maiden voyage from Southampton to New York","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titanic_(1997_film)","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Leonardo DiCaprio and Kate Winslet star as members of different social classes","ok":true}],"note":"Titanic var verdens største skib ved ibrugtagning, jomfrurejse i 1912, ramte et isbjerg, sank i Nordatlanten og kendes fra filmen fra 1997 med DiCaprio."},"who|Tivoli":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-08","sources":[{"u":"https://www.tivoli.dk/en/about-tivoli/the-history-of-tivoli-gardens","d":"tivoli.dk","q":"On 15 August 1843, the Gardens opened its gates to an enthralled public","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.kopenhagen.info/en/tivoli/","d":"kopenhagen.info","q":"Tivoli sits right in the centre of Copenhagen, next to Central Station","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.kopenhagen.info/en/tivoli/","d":"kopenhagen.info","q":"The star attraction is the wooden roller coaster Rutschebanen","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.kopenhagen.info/en/tivoli/","d":"kopenhagen.info","q":"after dark, hundreds of thousands of lights define its character","ok":true}],"note":"Tivoli åbnede 15. august 1843, ligger midt i København ved Hovedbanegården, har træ-rutsjebanen Rut