.dk/Google","d":"lex.dk","q":"Google, amerikansk teknologiselskab, grundlagt i Mountain View, Silicon Valley, Californien, i 1998 af Larry Page","ok":true}]},"tl|Den første McDonald's i Danmark (1981) | Den første McDonald's i Rusland (1990)":{"pool":"tl","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/McDonald's","d":"lex.dk","q":"Den første danske McDonald's blev åbnet i 1981.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald%27s_in_Russia","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The first McDonald's in the country had a grand opening on Moscow's Pushkin Square on 31 January 1990","ok":true}]},"tl|Emoji blev opfundet (1999) | Den første iPhone blev lanceret (2007)":{"pool":"tl","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emoji","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The more well-known DoCoMo emoji set was created by Shigetaka Kurita in 1999 for NTT DoCoMo's i-mode, used on its mobile platform.","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/iPhone","d":"lex.dk","q":"Den første iPhone blev lanceret af Apple i 2007","ok":true}]},"tl|Frugtfluerne – de første dyr i rummet (1947) | Laika – den første hund i kredsløb om Jorden (1957)":{"pool":"tl","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/space-astronomy/what-was-first-animal-space","d":"rmg.co.uk","q":"the first living creatures intentionally sent into space were fruit flies. These were transported aboard a V2 rocket on 20 February 1947.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.aps.org/apsnews/2023/01/fruit-flies-space","d":"aps.org","q":"Of course, the flies didn’t have much of a say when they blasted off on a V-2 rocket launched from New Mexico’s White Sands Proving Grounds on Feb. 20, 1947.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laika","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"she flew aboard the Sputnik 2 spacecraft, launched into low orbit on 3 November 1957","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/space-astronomy/what-was-first-animal-space","d":"rmg.co.uk","q":"The first animal to make an orbital spaceflight around the Earth was the dog Laika, aboard the Soviet spacecraft Sputnik 2 on 3 November 1957.","ok":true}]},"tl|Den første registrerede computerbug – en natsværmer i Harvard Mark II (1947) | Altair 8800 – den første succesfulde hjemmecomputer (1974)":{"pool":"tl","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/5927/First-computer-bug-is-found/","d":"computinghistory.org.uk","q":"On September 9th 1947, one of the team of engineers working on Harvard University’s Mark II computer recorded the first actual computer “bug” — a moth stuck between the r","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.si.edu/exhibitions/stalking-elusive-computer-bug%3Aevent-exhib-4182","q":"This showcase features the first, actual bug (a moth) found in a computing device at the Harvard Computational Lab in 1947","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bug","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"operators traced an error in the Mark II to a moth trapped in a relay. The moth was removed from the mechanism and taped in a log book with the note \"First actual case of","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altair_8800","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The Altair 8800 is a microcomputer introduced in 1974 by Micro Instrumentation and Telemetry Systems (MITS) based on the Intel 8080 CPU","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.computerhistory.org/revolution/artifact/352/1696","d":"computerhistory.org","q":"The basic Altair 8800 had only toggle switches and binary lights for input/output. Yet it was the first microcomputer to sell in large numbers: more than 5,000 in the fir","ok":true}]},"tl|Poulsen og Petersen viser filmlydsystemet (1923) | Første danske tonefilm: «Præsten i Vejlby» (1931)":{"pool":"tl","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dansk_film","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"De danske ingeniøre