","q":"The longest pizza measures 6,333 feet and was achieved by Pizzaovens.com, Venice Bakery, Orlando Foods, At-Pac, Sysco, TFX Non Stick, Capstone Scaffold Services, Scaffold","ok":true}]},"rec|Hvor tung var verdens tungeste vandmelon (Chris Kent, 2013)? (Guinness)":{"pool":"rec","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/heaviest-watermelon","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"The heaviest watermelon weighs 159 kg (350.5 lb) and was grown by Chris Kent (USA) of Sevierville, Tennessee, USA, as verified on 4 October 2013.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/watermelon-may-be-the-most-unnatural-yet-delicious-fruit","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"According to the Guinness World Records, the world's heaviest watermelon as of 2013, from the garden of Chris Kent of Sevierville, Tennessee, weighed a tad over 350 pound","ok":true}]},"rec|Hvor høj var verdens højeste isvaffel (Hennig-Olsen, 2015)? (Guinness)":{"pool":"rec","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/largest-ice-cream-cone","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"The tallest ice cream cone measures 3.08 m (10 ft 1.26 in) in height and was achieved by Hennig-Olsen Is AS and Trond L Wøien (both Norway) at Kristiansand, Norway, on 26","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.worldrecordacademy.com/food/tallest_ice_cream_cone_Norwegian_company_breaks_Guinness_World_Records_record_215416.html","d":"worldrecordacademy.com","q":"The Guinness World Records' record for the tallest ice cream cone measures 3.08 m (10 ft 1.26 in) in height and was achieved by Hennig-Olsen Is AL and Trond L Wøien (both","ok":true}]},"who|Mantisreje":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis_shrimp","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Compared with the four types of photoreceptor cell that humans possess in their eyes, the eyes of a mantis shrimp have between 12 and 16 types of photoreceptor cells.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/83127-most-sophisticated-eyes-of-any-animal","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"Their compound eyes, made up of thousands of repeating units called ommatidia, can contain as many as 12–16 different photoreceptors, compared to four in the human eye.","ok":true}]},"who|Narhval":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narwhal","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The most conspicuous trait of male narwhals is a long, spiralled tusk, which is a canine tooth that projects from the left side of the upper jaw.","ok":true},{"u":"https://oceanexplorer.noaa.gov/ocean-fact/narwhal","d":"oceanexplorer.noaa.gov","q":"male narwhals have a single long, straight tooth (or tusk) that protrudes two to three meters out of the upper left jaw.","ok":true}]},"who|Kakapo":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakapo","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"It is the world's only flightless parrot, the world's heaviest parrot, and also is nocturnal, herbivorous, visibly sexually dimorphic in body size","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/447093-heaviest-parrot","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"The world's heaviest species of parrot is the kākāpo ( Strigops habroptilus ), aka the owl parrot, nowadays confined in the wild to three tiny islets off the two major is","ok":true}]},"who|Tardigrad":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-13","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Tardigrades live in diverse regions of Earth's biosphere: mountaintops, the deep sea, tropical rainforests, and the Antarctic.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Human_and_Robotic_Exploration/Research/