.org/wiki/Pangolin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Pangolins can emit a noxious-smelling chemical from glands near the anus, similar to the spray of a skunk.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Manis/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"When threatened, they roll into a ball, leaving only their hardened scaly exterior exposed which deters predation.","ok":true}]},"who|Dovendyr":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-15","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They spend 90 percent of their time motionless.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The shaggy coat has grooved hair that is host to symbiotic green algae which camouflage sloths in the trees and provide it nutrients.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths descend about once every eight days to defecate on the ground.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths can reduce their already slow metabolism even further and slow their heart rate to less than a third of normal, allowing them to hold their breath underwater for u","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths are almost helpless on the ground but are able to swim.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Bradypus_variegatus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Brown-throated three-toed sloths descend from the canopy to defecate and urinate on the ground. Although they only descend from the canopy once every 3 to 8 days, this be","ok":true}]},"who|Aye-aye":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-15","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aye-aye","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"It is the world's largest nocturnal primate.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aye-aye","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"taps on the trunks and branches of trees at a rate of up to eight times pe