ngated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/the-miracle-of-bananas","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"the fruit itself is a berry.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad er en jordbær botanisk set IKKE?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/your-shot-berries-are-in-season-and-on-the-menu","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"strawberry (not technically a berry, but that’s okay)","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken krig er den korteste i historien (ca. 38-45 min)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Zanzibar_War","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The conflict lasted between 38 and 45 minutes, marking it as the shortest recorded war in history.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.forcesnews.com/news/was-shortest-ever-war-military-history","d":"forcesnews.com","q":"Lasting between 38 and 45 minutes, according to differing reports, the Anglo-Zanzibar War took place on the morning of 27 August 1896.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket lille dyr overlevede som det første i det åbne rum?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tardigrade","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They have survived exposure to outer space.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Human_and_Robotic_Exploration/Research/Tiny_animals_survive_exposure_to_space","d":"esa.int","q":"Scientists recently revealed that tiny creatures called water bears are the first animals to survive exposure to space.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor længe kan en kakerlak leve uden hoved (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"source