day (sol) is equal to 24.6 hours.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/asset/hubble/mars-near-2016-opposition","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"A Martian day is about 24 hours and 37 minutes.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken fødevare er fundet spiselig i oldgamle grave?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"when properly stored, honey therefore does not spoil.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20250701-the-chemical-secrets-that-help-keep-honey-fresh-for-so-long","d":"bbc.com","q":"Honey is a natural sweetener, and bacteria loves to feast on sugar. But honey is remarkably resistant to spoilage.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad er ældre: undervisning ved Oxford eller Aztekerriget?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Oxford","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"There is evidence of teaching as early as 1096","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-19828041","d":"bbc.com","q":"1428-1521 - The latest of a long line of indigenous civilisations, the Aztec Empire - an alliance of Nahuatl-speaking city states led by Tenochtitlan - establishes hegemo","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor optrådte ordet «nerd» første gang?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nerd","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The first documented appearance of the word nerd is as the name of a creature in Dr. Seuss's book If I Ran the Zoo (1950)","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nerd","d":"en.wiktionary.org","q":"The word, capitalized, appeared in 1950 in Dr. Seuss’s If I Ran the Zoo as the name of an imaginary animal:","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad sker der med astronauters højde i rummet?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Human_and_Robotic_Exploration/Astronauts/Living_in_space","d":"esa.int","q":"without the compressive force of gravity, your spinal column expands and you grow taller, usually by between 5 and 8 cm.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/whatisyourspaceheight.pdf","d":"nasa.gov","q":"NASA has found that the height of astronauts increases approximately 3% over the first 3 to 4 days of weightlessness in space.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvem levede tættere på månelandingen end på pyramidernes bygning?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/so-cleopatra-lived-closer-in-time-to-the-first-lunar-landing-than-the-great-pyramids.html","d":"worldatlas.com","q":"Cleopatra was born ~2,500 years after the Great Pyramid at Giza was built, and ~2,000 years before the first lunar landing.","ok":true},{"u":"https://commonplacefacts.com/2019/11/15/cleopatra-moon-landing-pyramid/","d":"commonplacefacts.com","q":"Cleopatra is closer in time to the moon landing than she is to the Great Pyramid.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad farve er en isbjørns hud under pelsen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The polar bear is white or yellowish-furred with black skin and a thick layer of fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"It has black skin under the white fur.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Kan en skildpadde komme ud af sit skjold?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The carapace is fused with the vertebrae and ribs while the plastron is formed from bones of the shoulder girdle, sternum, and gastralia (abdominal ribs).","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"The inside of a turtle's shell has about 60 bones. It includes parts of the spine and ribs, meaning the turtle cannot crawl out of its shell.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken fugl kan flyve baglæns?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummingbird","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Hummingbirds have compact bodies with relatively long, bladelike wings having anatomical structure enabling helicopter-like flight in any direction, including the ability","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummingbird","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They are also the only group of birds able to fly backwards.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har blåt blod?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horseshoe_crab","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rather than using iron-based hemoglobin, horseshoe crabs transport oxygen with a copper-based protein called hemocyanin, giving its blood a bright blue color.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/animal-blood-comes-in-a-rainbow-of-colors","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The milky-blue, hemocyanin-rich blood of Atlantic horseshoe crabs, for instance, clots when it comes in contact with bacterial toxins.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en mus?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://a-z-animals.com/animals/mouse/mouse-teeth-everything-you-need-to-know/","d":"a-z-animals.com","q":"Mice have 16 teeth in their mouth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sfzoodocents.org/notebook/FactSheets/MAMMALIA/RodentiaLagomorphs/HouseMouse.pdf","d":"sfzoodocents.org","q":"Mice have 16 teeth: 4 incisor and 12 molars.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr kan trække vejret gennem endetarmen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/science/the-secret-to-turtle-hibernation-butt-breathing","d":"pbs.org","q":"turtles really can breathe through their butts","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/turtles-breathe-butts/","d":"snopes.com","q":"Some species of turtles can breathe out of their cloaca when under water.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Kan en frø overleve, selv om den fryser til is?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/how-do-frogs-survive-wint/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"A partially frozen frog will stop breathing, and its heart will stop beating. It will appear quite dead. But when the hibernaculum warms up above freezing, the frog's fro","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/32175-can-frogs-survive-being-frozen.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Fortunately for them, they don’t freeze to death: Most survive to mate another spring.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad er størst hos en struds – øjet eller hjernen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/516757-largest-eyes-for-a-bird","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"The diameter of an ostrich eye measured from the centre of the cornea at the front of the eye to the centre of the retina at the back can be up to 50 mm, which is larger ","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/uk/discover/animals/birds/ostrich-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"Ostriches huge eyes (which are bigger than their brains!) give them excellent eyesight","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor meget vejer en blåhvals tunge (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Their tongues alone can weigh as much as an elephant.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/83817-heaviest-tongue","d":"guinnessworldrecords.com","q":"The