post.com","q":"certain species of land snails can go without food or movement for up to three years","ok":true},{"u":"https://snailpedia.com/how-long-do-snails-sleep/","d":"snailpedia.com","q":"Snails don’t sleep for three years in the ordinary sense.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange gange i minuttet slår et kolibris hjerte under flyvning (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.audubon.org/news/hummingbird-hearts-beat-10-times-faster-yours","d":"audubon.org","q":"An active hummingbird’s heart pumps at 1,200 beats per minute","ok":true},{"u":"https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/articles/hummingbirds-in-the-garden/","d":"hort.extension.wisc.edu","q":"heart rate up to 1,260 beats per minute","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange knogler er der i en girafs hals?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Like all mammals, giraffes have only seven bones in their necks.","ok":true},{"u":"https://savegiraffesnow.org/how-many-vertebrae-do-giraffes-have/","d":"savegiraffesnow.org","q":"Giraffes have seven cervical vertebrae, the same number of neck bones as humans and most other mammals.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvorfor skifter en kameleon farve?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Most can change the colour of their skins for camouflage, or to signal mood to other chameleons.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/article/chameleons-color-change-mimicry-science","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"the skin’s changing hue is in fact a physiological reaction that’s mostly for communication.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange arme har en søstjerne typisk?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Starfish typically have a central disc and usually five arms, though some species have a larger number of arms.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starfish","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Most starfish have five arms","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr sover med ét øje åbent?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/meet-the-animals-that-literally-sleep-with-one-eye-open/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"the animals keep only one eye closed during their daily rest.","ok":true},{"u":"https://news.cnrs.fr/opinions/cetaceans-keep-an-eye-open","d":"news.cnrs.fr","q":"John Lilly was the first to experimentally study dolphins, starting in 1964. He observed that these mammals sleep with one eye open.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange maver har en fugl?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://bio.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Introductory_and_General_Biology/General_Biology_(Boundless)/34%3A_Animal_Nutrition_and_the_Digestive_System/34.04%3A_Digestive_Systems_-_Vertebrate_Digestive_Systems","d":"bio.libretexts.org","q":"The stomach of birds has two chambers","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Their stomach comes next, with two very different parts.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en gris?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pig","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The dental formula of adult pigs is 3.1.4.3 3.1.4.3, giving a total of 44 teeth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://askavet.com/blogs/news/how-many-teeth-do-pigs-have-and-what-are-they-called","d":"askavet.com","q":"Adult pigs usually have 44 teeth","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en ko?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://veterinaryanatomy.com/atlas/head-neck/splanchnology/teeth-and-age-determination-by-dentition/","d":"veterinaryanatomy.com","q":"Permanent: 2(I 0/3, C 0/1, P 3/3, M 3/3) = 32 teeth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.clovermeadowsbeef.com/cows-have-teeth/","d":"clovermeadowsbeef.com","q":"Mature cattle have a total of 32 teeth","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en alligator (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/american-alligator","d":"nationalzoo.si.edu","q":"Alligators have between 74 and 80 teeth in their mouth at a time.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencefocus.com/nature/whats-the-difference-between-an-alligator-and-a-crocodile","d":"sciencefocus.com","q":"With 80 teeth, alligators have more chompers than their crocodile counterparts","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder kan en alligator have i løbet af sit liv?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/american-alligator","d":"nationalzoo.si.edu","q":"An alligator can go through 3,000 teeth in a lifetime.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.aucklandzoo.co.nz/animals/american-alligator","d":"aucklandzoo.co.nz","q":"they have up to 80 teeth in their mouth at any one time, and can have up to 3,000 teeth throughout their lifetime!","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en rotte?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://veteriankey.com/60-small-mammal-dentistry/","d":"veteriankey.com","q":"Rat, hamster (golden and Russian): 2 × (I 1/1; C 0/0; P 0/0; M 3/3) = 16","ok":true},{"u":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7128658/","d":"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","q":"Muridae (Old World rats and mice) have the following dental formula:1/1 0/0 0/0 3/3=16","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en have-snegl (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"so