arieties are the most common, hence their name, but species with 10, 20, and even 40 arms exist.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange planeter i vores solsystem har ringe?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ring_system","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Jupiter's ring system was the third to be discovered, when it was first observed by the Voyager 1 probe in 1979, and was observed more thoroughly by the Galileo orbiter i","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasas-webb-telescope-will-study-jupiter-its-rings-and-two-intriguing-moons/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"All four of the gas giant planets of the solar system have rings, with Saturn’s being the most prominent.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange officielt anerkendte dværgplaneter er der i vores solsystem?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_System","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The International Astronomical Union describes the Solar System as all objects that are bound by the gravity of the Sun, the Sun itself, its eight planets, and the other ","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"Our solar system has eight planets: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune. There are five officially recognized dwarf planets in our solar sys","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange knogler har en nyfødt baby (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_skeleton","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The human skeleton is the internal framework of the human body. It is composed of around 270 bones at birth – this total decreases to around 206 bones by adulthood after ","ok":true},{"u":"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/25176-bones","d":"my.clevelandclinic.org","q":"Babies are usually born with 270 bones that grow together and fuse into their adult skeleton.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en fugl (voksen)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_bird_genera","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"characterised by feathers, a beak with no teeth, the laying of hard-shelled eggs, and a high metabolic rate.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owls","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Toothless like other birds, owls swallow their victims whole.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange lunger har et menneske?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lung","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Humans have two lungs, a right lung and a left lung.","ok":true},{"u":"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/8960-lungs","d":"my.clevelandclinic.org","q":"You have two lungs, a right and a left.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr kan ikke kaste op?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rabbits cannot vomit","ok":true},{"u":"https://vcahospitals.com/know-your-pet/rabbits-problems","d":"vcahospitals.com","q":"Since bunnies cannot vomit","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr sover ofte med åbne øjne?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rabbits are typically nocturnal and often sleep with their eyes open.","ok":true},{"u":"https://rabbit.org/health/the-rabbit-eye-a-complete-guide/","d":"rabbit.org","q":"bunnies can also sleep without fully closing their eyes, essentially sleeping with them open.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr kan næsten se hele vejen rundt om sig?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the rabbit has a panoramic field of vision that encompasses nearly 360 degrees.","ok":true},{"u":"https://rabbit.org/health/what-do-rabbits-see/","d":"rabbit.org","q":"allowing the rabbit to see nearly 360 degrees","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har ingen tårekanaler?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Goats have no tear ducts.","ok":true},{"u":"https://extension.purdue.edu/county/decatur/_docs/mini-4-h-goats.pdf","d":"extension.purdue.edu","q":"Goats have no tear ducts.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr kan holde vejret i op til 40 minutter under vand?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths can reduce their already slow metabolism even further and slow their heart rate to less than a third of normal, allowing them to hold their breath underwater for u","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zqk4qyc","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Sloths can also hold their breath underwater for as long as 40 minutes.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har ikke 7 halsknogler, som de fleste pattedyr?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths are unusual among mammals in not having seven cervical vertebrae.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Choloepus_hoffmanni/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"One of the most constant mammalian morphological characteristics is the presence of seven cervical vertebrae.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har grønne alger i pelsen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The shaggy coat has grooved hair that is host to symbiotic green algae","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Choloepus_hoffmanni/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Algae grows on the fur of C. hoffmanni","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har en tunge, der er længere end kroppen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"While the chameleons' tongues are typically thought to be one and a half to two times the length of their bodies","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Chamaeleo_chamaeleon/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"They also have unique tongues, which can be as long as their bodies","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har sort hud under den hvide pels?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The polar bear is white or yellowish-furred with black skin and a thick layer of fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/polar-bear","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"But under their fur, polar bears have black skin—the better to soak in the sun's warming rays.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har den tætteste pels i verden?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_otter","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With up to 150,000 strands of hair per square centimetre (970,000/in2), its fur is the densest of any animal.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Enhydra_lutris/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Sea otter fur is the densest of all mammals, with about 100,000 hairs per square centimeter.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor hurtigt kan en struds løbe?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With the ability to run at 70 km/h (43 mph), they are the fastest birds on land.","ok":true},{"u":"https://nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/news/how-fast-ostrich-and-more-fun-facts","d":"nationalzoo.si.edu","q":"Scientists have seen ostriches run continuously at speeds of 30-37 mph and sprint up to 43 mph.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har ingen tænder?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anteater","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The mouth is small and has no teeth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Myrmecophaga_tridactyla/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Giant anteaters have no teeth.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken af disse frugter er botanisk set et bær?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.lsop.colostate.edu/2020/04/29/everything-you-need-to-know-is-that-a-berry","d":"lsop.colostate.edu","q":"pumpkins, oranges, and bananas are all berries.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor langt kan en ugle dreje sit hoved?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Owls can rotate their heads and necks as much as 270°.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owls","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange gange i minuttet kan en myresluger slikke med tungen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anteater","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The tongue is attached to the sternum and moves very quickly, flicking 150 times per minute.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Myrmecophaga_tridactyla/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"The tongue is attached to the sternum and moves very quickly, flicking 150 times per minute.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har vandrette, spalteformede pupiller?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Goats have horizontal, slit-shaped pupils","ok":true},{"u":"https://extension.purdue.edu/county/decatur/_docs/mini-4-h-goats.pdf","d":"extension.purdue.edu","q":"Goats have horizontal pupils.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har flest tænder?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snail","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most snails have thousands of microscopic tooth-like structures located on a banded ribbon-like tongue called a radula.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/z9yv6rd","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"the snail, which has thousands upon thousands of teeth on their tongue.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har en snabel uden knogler?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"This versatile appendage contains up to 150,000 separate muscle fascicles, with no bone and little fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/african-elephant","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"An elephant's trunk is controlled by many muscles.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket pattedyr lægger æg?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platypus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Together with the four species of echidna, it is one of the five extant species of monotremes, mammals that lay eggs instead of giving birth to live young.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/platypus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"It is one of only two mammals (the echidna is the other) that lay eggs.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har en pels, der er gennemsigtig?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ursus_maritimus","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"the fur is actually clear, lacking in pigment","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/animals-skin-colors-zebras-big-cats","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The hair, if you take a couple of strands, looks clear","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har en sort tunge?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe's tongue is about 45 cm (18 in) long. It is black, perhaps to protect against sunburn, and can grasp foliage and delicately pick off leaves.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They have a long black tongue, up to 45 cm in length.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken farve har en citron?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The lemon tree produces a pointed oval yellow fruit.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"A lemon is a yellow citrus fruit.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad spiser en giraf?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their food source is leaves, fruits, and flowers of woody plants, primarily acacia species, which they browse at heights most other ground-based herbivores cannot reach.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Giraffes eat mostly leaves from tall trees, which they can reach because of their long legs and long necks, as well as fruit.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad spiser en elefant?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They are herbivorous, and they stay near water when it is accessible.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"African elephants are larger and have bigger ears. They are grazers who still do a lot of browsing: they eat leaves, branches and grass.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad kalder man en baby-får?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheep","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"and a young sheep as a lamb.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestic_sheep","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Young sheep are called lambs.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad kalder man en baby-ged?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Juvenile goats are called kids, a term derived from a Scandinavian language, such as Old Norse kið/kith, with the same meaning.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestic_goat","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Young goats are called kids.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har ingen ben?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Snakes are limbless reptiles of the squamate suborder Serpentes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They are carnivores, with long narrow bodies and no legs.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr lever i vandet?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate with a tough cranium to protect the brain.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Fish (plural: fish or fishes) are a group of animals which live in water and respire (get oxygen) from their gills.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad spiser en kanin?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They are familiar throughout the world as a small herbivore, a prey animal, a domesticated form of livestock, and a pet, having a widespread effect on ecologies and cultu","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They live in families and eat vegetables and hay.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har fjer?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Birds are vertebrate animals constituting the class Aves, characterised by feathers, toothless beaked jaws, the laying of hard-shelled eggs, a high metabolic rate, a four","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Their feathers help prevent loss of body heat.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad bruger vi øjnene til?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"The eye is a round organ for sensing light so organisms can see.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad bruger vi ørerne til?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ear","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In vertebrates, an ear is the organ that enables hearing and (in mammals) body balance using the vestibular system.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ear","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"The ear is the part of the body which allows animals (including people) to hear.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvad bruger vi næsen til?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nose","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"as well as enabling the sensory perception of smell.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nose","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"A nose is a body part which allows animals to smell things.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr lever i Afrika og er det højeste?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Giraffes (genus Giraffa) are large African hoofed mammals. They are the tallest living terrestrial animals and the largest ruminants on Earth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe (Giraffa camelopardalis) is a mammal which lives in Africa. Giraffes have an even number of toes and are the tallest land animals.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang er en girafs tunge?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe's tongue is about 45 cm (18 in) long. It is black, perhaps to protect against sunburn, and can grasp foliage and delicately pick off leaves.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They have a long black tongue, up to 45 cm in length.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr spiser blade fra træer?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their food source is leaves, fruits, and flowers of woody plants, primarily acacia species, which they browse at heights most other ground-based herbivores cannot reach.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Giraffes eat mostly leaves from tall trees, which they can reach because of their long legs and long necks, as well as fruit.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr spiser græs og blade?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They are herbivorous, and they stay near water when it is accessible.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"African elephants are larger and have bigger ears. They are grazers who still do a lot of browsing: they eat leaves, branches and grass.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken farve har en tomat?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomato","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Most tomatoes are red, but are green when unripe.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomato","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Modern varieties have been bred to ripen uniformly red, in a process that has impaired the fruit's sweetness and flavor.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken farve har himlen på en klar dag?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"On a clear day the sky appears blue.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The daytime sky appears blue because air molecules scatter shorter wavelengths of sunlight more than longer ones (redder light).","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har en lang tunge?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe's tongue is about 45 cm (18 in) long. It is black, perhaps to protect against sunburn, and can grasp foliage and delicately pick off leaves.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They have a long black tongue, up to 45 cm in length.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr er verdens hurtigste på land?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheetah","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The cheetah is a pursuit predator and the fastest land animal, capable of running at 93–104 km/h","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/cheetah","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The cheetah is the world's fastest land mammal.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken planet er varmest i solsystemet?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"At the mean surface level, the atmosphere reaches a temperature of 737 K (464 °C; 867 °F), making it the hottest planet in the solar system and also a pressure 92 times g","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.timeanddate.com/astronomy/planets/venus.html","d":"timeanddate.com","q":"the average surface temperature is about 480 degrees Celsius (900 degrees Fahrenheit)—making it the hottest planet in the solar system.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor stor en del af en voksen mands krop er vand (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_body","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The adult male body is about 60% total body water content of some 42 litres","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.usgs.gov/water-science-school/science/water-you-water-and-human-body","d":"usgs.gov","q":"Up to 60% of the human adult body is water.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange timer sover en koala om dagen (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They are largely sedentary and sleep up to twenty hours a day.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/koala","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Tucked into forks or nooks in the trees, koalas may sleep for 18 to 22 hours.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange grader kan en ugle dreje hovedet?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Owls can rotate their heads and necks as much as 270°.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"they make up for their lack of ocular musculature with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang er en girafs tunge (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe's tongue is about 45 cm (18 in) long.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/giraffe","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"They simply use their 18-inch (46-centimeter) tongue and prehensile lips to reach around the thorns.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr har de største øjne i verden?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colossal_squid","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The colossal squid has the largest eyes of any documented animal, with an estimated diameter of 27–30 cm (11–12 in)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.oceana.org/marine-life/colossal-squid/","d":"oceana.org","q":"recorded eye diameters reaching just shy of 30 centimeters (11.8 inches)","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor meget kan en kæmpeblæksprutte veje (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colossal_squid","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The species is confirmed to have a mass of at least 495 kilograms (1,091 lb)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.oceana.org/marine-life/colossal-squid/","d":"oceana.org","q":"weigh nearly 500 kg (1,100 lbs)","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang kan en kameleons tunge være i forhold til kroppen?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"While the chameleons' tongues are typically thought to be one and a half to two times the length of their bodies","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/reptiles/facts/chameleon","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Twice its body length, a chameleon’s sticky, projectile tongue is an evolutionary marvel used to catch prey.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Kan en kameleon se ultraviolet lys?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Chameleons can see in both visible and ultraviolet light.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/reptiles/facts/chameleon","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Chameleons can see a wide range of colors, from ultraviolet to infrared.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor mange tænder har en voksen (menneske)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_tooth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Humans usually have 20 primary (deciduous, \"baby\" or \"milk\") teeth and 32 permanent (adult) teeth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.healthline.com/health/how-many-teeth-do-adults-have","d":"healthline.com","q":"Adults have 32 teeth.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor meget vejer et menneskehjerte (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"An adult heart has a mass of 250–350 grams (9–12 oz).","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.healthline.com/health/heart","d":"healthline.com","q":"The average human heart weighs between 6 and 11 ounces.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilken planet har Den Store Røde Plet (en kæmpe storm)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Red_Spot","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The Great Red Spot is a persistent, elliptical high-pressure region in the atmosphere of the planet Jupiter, producing the largest anticyclonic storm in the Solar System.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.timeanddate.com/astronomy/planets/jupiter.html","d":"timeanddate.com","q":"A prominent feature is the Great Red Spot, a storm that is bigger than Earth and hundreds of years old.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvilket dyr er det eneste pattedyr, der kan flyve?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Bats are winged mammals, the only mammals capable of true and sustained flight.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nwf.org/Educational-Resources/Wildlife-Guide/Mammals/Bats","d":"nwf.org","q":"Bats are the only mammals that can fly.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang tid tager det Venus at dreje én gang rundt (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Venusian sidereal day, 243 Earth days, lasts longer than a Venusian year, 224.7 Earth days.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.timeanddate.com/astronomy/planets/venus.html","d":"timeanddate.com","q":"it takes around 243 Earth days to complete one spin","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang er et år på Venus (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Venusian year, 224.7 Earth days.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.timeanddate.com/astronomy/planets/venus.html","d":"timeanddate.com","q":"A tropical year on Venus is approximately 225 Earth days.","ok":true}]},"kquiz|Hvor lang er et døgn på Venus (ca.)?":{"pool":"kquiz","status":"bekræftet",