-shiny-192424","d":"theconversation.com","q":"Snails also leave a chemical trail in their mucus that other snails can use to find them, such as when they are looking for a mate.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Fisk kan høre.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Hearing too is an important sensory system in fish.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2003/02/030210075908.htm","d":"sciencedaily.com","q":"With ears similar to those of other vertebrates, including mammals, most fish use hearing to sense their acoustic environment.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Den blå hval er verdens største dyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The blue whale is the largest animal known ever to have existed.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Blue whales are the largest animals ever known to have lived on Earth.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En haj kan udskifte tænder.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Shark teeth are embedded in the gums rather than directly affixed to the jaw, and are constantly replaced throughout life.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/shark","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Formidable predators, sharks have mouths lined with multiple rows of individual teeth that fall out and grow back on a routine basis.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bier danser for at vise vej.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.