kke gå baglæns.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.australia.com/en/things-to-do/wildlife/kangaroo-interesting-facts.html","d":"australia.com","q":"Because of their long feet and large tail, kangaroos can’t walk or hop backwards.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencekids.co.nz/sciencefacts/animals/kangaroo.html","d":"sciencekids.co.nz","q":"Kangaroos can’t walk backwards.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En giraf har samme antal halsknogler som et menneske.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The long neck results from a disproportionate lengthening of the cervical vertebrae, not from the addition of more vertebrae.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zskkfdm","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Despite its long appearance, the neck of a giraffe is actually made up of just seven bones!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan dreje hovedet helt rundt.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Owls can rotate their heads and necks as much as 270°.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/how-owls-twist-heads-almost-360-degrees","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"owls can rotate their necks a maximum of 270 degrees","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda spiser næsten kun bambus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"bamboo accounts for 99 percent of their diets.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/wildlife/giant-pandas","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"bamboo, which is 99% 