e","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"stomach with four compartments; the rumen","ok":true},{"u":"https://extension.msstate.edu/publications/understanding-the-ruminant-animal-digestive-system","d":"extension.msstate.edu","q":"True ruminants, such as cattle, sheep, goats, deer, and antelope, have one stomach with four compartments","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et næsehornshorn er lavet af det samme stof som hår og negle.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoceros","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same material as hair and fingernails","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/rhinoceros","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"A rhino’s horn is made of keratin, the same material that makes up our fingernails and hair.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En frø kan trække vejret gennem huden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frog","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"gas exchange across the skin","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/animals/frogs/how-do-frogs-breathe-and-drink-through-their-skin","d":"livescience.com","q":"can use its skin to both breathe and drink.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala spiser mest eukalyptusblade.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the leaves of these trees make up most of their diet.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.australia.com/en/things-to-do/wildlife/facts-about-koalas.html","d":"australia.com","q":"Koalas survive on a diet of eucalyptus leaves and can eat up to a kilogram (over two pounds) a day!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Sommerfugle smager med fødderne.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Sommerfugle har smagssans på fødderne.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfly","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A butterfly's sense of taste is coordinated by chemoreceptors on the tarsi, or feet, which work only on contact","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/a-monarch-butterflys-3000-mile-journey-wild-critters-usa/35090/","d":"pbs.org","q":"That's right, butterflies can taste with their feet.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et næsehorns horn er lavet af hår.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Næsehornshorn består af keratin, ligesom hår og negle.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoceros","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same material as hair and fingernails","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.savetherhino.org/our-work/protecting-rhinos/what-is-rhino-horn-made-of/","d":"savetherhino.org","q":"rhino horn is composed primarily of keratin, a protein also found in human hair and fingernails.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Isbjørne har sort hud under den hvide pels.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Isbjørnens hud er sort, og pelsen er gennemsigtig.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The polar bear is white or yellowish-furred with black skin and a thick layer of fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/fascinating-facts/polar-bears","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"Beneath all that thick fur, polar bears have jet black skin.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En haj har ingen knogler – kun brusk.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Hajers skelet består af brusk, ikke ben.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sharks and other cartilaginous fish (skates and rays) have skeletons made of cartilage and connective tissue.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/quick-questions/do-sharks-have-bones.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"Sharks don't have bones. Their skeletons are made of cartilage","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Krokodiller kan ikke svede.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Krokodiller har ingen svedkirtler.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Crocodiles do not have sweat glands and release heat through their mouths.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/crocodilian?qt-animals_page_content_tabs=1","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"These reptiles do not have sweat glands and may release heat through their mouth by mouth gaping, similar to a dog panting.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En giraf har kun 7 halsvirvler.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Giraffens hals er lang, fordi virvlerne er lange – ikke fordi der er flere.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The long neck results from a disproportionate lengthening of the cervical vertebrae, not from the addition of more vertebrae.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/how-is-a-mouse-like-a-giraffe.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"Despite its elongated form, the neck of a giraffe is made up of just seven large bones known as cervical vertebrae.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En krokodille kan ikke stikke tungen ud.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Krokodillens tunge er bundet fast i munden.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their tongues are not free, but held in place by a membrane that limits movement; as a result, crocodiles are unable to stick out their tongues.","ok":true},{"u":"https://metro.co.uk/2017/10/22/can-a-crocodile-stick-out-its-tongue-odd-difference-between-alligators-and-crocs-7015099/","d":"metro.co.uk","q":"It turns out crocodiles can't stick their tongues out, while alligators can.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Slanger lugter med tungen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Slanger bruger tungen til at samle duftstoffer.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Snakes rely heavily on their sense of smell to track prey. They collect particles from the air, ground, or water using their forked tongue, which are then transferred to ","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/snakes-senses-stretchy-jaws-deadly-venom.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"pick up odour molecules from their environment. When they retract their tongue, the molecules pass into the vomeronasal organ in the roof of their mouth, delivering smell","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Delfiner sover med kun den ene hjernehalvdel ad gangen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Den anden halvdel holder vejret og vagt.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Generally, dolphins sleep with only one brain hemisphere in slow-wave sleep at a time, thus maintaining enough consciousness to breathe and to watch for possible predator","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/article/can-animals-survive-without-sleep/","d":"pbs.org","q":"dolphins sleep, they shut down only one hemisphere of the brain at a time. The other half of the brain stays awake to keep the dolphin","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flamingoer er lyserøde, fordi de spiser rejer og alger.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Farven kommer fra carotenoider i føden.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The pink or reddish colour of flamingos comes from carotenoids in their diet of animal and plant plankton.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/flamingo","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"The flamingo's pink or reddish color comes from the rich sources of carotenoid pigments (like the pigments of carrots) in the algae and small crustaceans the birds eat.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Pingviner kan ikke flyve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"Pingviner bruger vingerne som svømmefødder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Penguins are a group of flightless semi-aquatic sea birds which live almost exclusively in the Southern Hemisphere.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/group/birds/penguins","d":"pbs.org","q":"Penguins are flightless seabirds in the order Sphenisciformes (family Spheniscidae) that live almost entirely in the Southern Hemisphere.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flagermus er de eneste pattedyr, der kan flyve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Andre pattedyr kan kun glide, ikke flyve.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Bats are the only mammals capable of sustained flight","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/bat","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"Bats are the only mammals capable of true flight.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hvaler trækker vejret gennem et åndehul på toppen af hovedet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Åndehullet er en næseåbning på toppen af hovedet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/index.php/animals/whale","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"Toothed whales have one blowhole (adapted nostril) on top of the head that divides into two nostrils inside the head.","ok":true},{"u":"https://pbs.org/wnet/nature/ocean-giants-whale-fact-sheet/7567","d":"pbs.org","q":"Blowholes are nasal openings located at the top of a whale's head.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kameleoner kan bevæge øjnene uafhængigt af hinanden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"De kan se to retninger på én gang.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Chameleons' eyes are independently mobile","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/chameleon","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"their eyes, which can be moved independently of each other.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koalaer sover op til 20 timer om dagen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"Koalaen sover meget for at spare energi.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Koalas are largely sedentary and sleep up to twenty hours a day.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/koala","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"They don't get many calories from their diet, but they conserve energy by moving occasionally and by sleeping as much as 20 hours each day.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blæksprutte har 3 hjerter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"To hjerter pumper blod til gællerne, ét til kroppen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/octopuses-keep-surprising-us-here-are-eight-examples-how.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"They have blue blood, three hearts and a doughnut-shaped brain.","ok":true},{"u":"https://pbs.org/wnet/nature/group/other-species/octopus","d":"pbs.org","q":"Octopuses have three hearts (two pump blood through the gills; one circulates oxygenated blood through the body) and blue blood that uses the copper-based oxygen carrier ","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Blæksprutter har tre hjerter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Blæksprutter har to gællehjerter og ét hovedhjerte.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They have three hearts; a systemic or main heart that circulates blood around the body and two branchial or gill hearts that pump it through the two gills.","ok":true},{"u":"https://education.nationalgeographic.org/resource/animals-101-octopuses/","d":"education.nationalgeographic.org","q":"Their cardiovascular system includes three hearts, two pump blood to the gills and a third moves blood throughout the rest of the body.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bananer er bær.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Bananer er botanisk set bær.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/did-you-know/bananas-are-berries-raspberries-are-not","d":"mcgill.ca","q":"bananas, pumpkins, avocados and cucumbers are","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Jorden er perfekt rund.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Jorden er lidt flad ved polerne, så den er en ellipsoide.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Earth is rounded into an ellipsoid with a circumference of about 40,000 km","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"With an equatorial diameter of 7,926 miles (12,756 kilometers), Earth is the biggest of the terrestrial planets","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Venus er den varmeste planet i solsystemet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Venus er varmere end Merkur, selv om den ligger længere fra Solen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"making it the hottest planet in the solar system","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/venus/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"It’s the hottest planet in our solar system","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Lyn slår aldrig ned samme sted to gange.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Lyn kan sagtens slå ned samme sted flere gange.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the idea that lightning never strikes the same place twice is a common myth. In fact, lightning can, and often does, strike the same place more than once","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.weather.gov/safety/lightning-myths","d":"weather.gov","q":"Lightning often strikes the same place repeatedly","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Mennesker bruger kun 10 procent af hjernen.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Vi bruger stort set hele hjernen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten_percent_of_the_brain_myth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the physiology of brain mapping suggests that all areas of the brain have a function and that they are used nearly all the time","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/do-people-only-use-10-percent-of-their-brains/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"we use virtually every part of the brain","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Rejer har hjertet i hovedet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Rejens hjerte sidder i hovedet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Shrimp are widespread and abundant.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.niehs.nih.gov/health/kids/games/riddles/jokes/fun-facts-and-trivia","d":"niehs.nih.gov","q":"A shrimp's heart is in its head.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Strudse stikker hovedet i sandet, når de er bange.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Strudse graver redehuller i sandet, men stikker ikke hovedet i.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Ostriches do not have teeth, and like other birds, swallow sand and pebbles to grind food in their stomachs.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/uk/discover/animals/birds/ostrich-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"Have you ever heard that ostriches bury their head in the sand to hide? Well, as funny as that sounds, it's not true!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Skildpadder kan trække vejret gennem enden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Nogle skildpadder kan optage ilt gennem kloakken.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Some species can respire through the cloaca, which contains large sacs that are lined with many finger-like projections that take up dissolved oxygen from the water.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/did-you-know/turtles-breathe-out-their-butt","d":"mcgill.ca","q":"Technically the term is cloacal respiration","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Dovendyr kan holde vejret længere end delfiner.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Dovendyr kan holde vejret i op til 40 minutter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths can reduce their already slow metabolism even further and slow their heart rate to less than a third of normal, allowing them to hold their breath underwater for u","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zqk4qyc","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Sloths can also hold their breath underwater for as long as 40 minutes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kameler gemmer vand i puklen.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Puklen indeholder fedt, ikke vand.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"It is a common myth that a camel stores water in its hump, but the humps in fact are reservoirs of fatty tissue","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.clevelandzoosociety.org/z/2021/04/06/truth-or-tail-a-camels-hump","d":"clevelandzoosociety.org","q":"A camel's hump stores fat, not water.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Okser bliver sure, når de ser rød farve.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Okser er farveblinde for rød og reagerer på bevægelse.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A common misconception widely repeated in depictions of bull behavior is that the colour red angers bulls, inciting them to charge. In fact, like most mammals, cattle are","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/33700-bulls-charge-red.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Bulls, along with all other cattle, are color-blind to red.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flagermus er blinde.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Flagermus kan godt se.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Microbats tend to have small eyes but are still sensitive to light, and no species is truly blind.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/au/discover/animals/general-animals/bat-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"this old saying is totally inaccurate, as bats have good eyesight as well as awesome hearing","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Slanger kan ikke blinke.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Slanger har ingen øjenlåg, kun en gennemsigtig skæl.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The eyelids of a snake are transparent 'spectacle' scales, also known as brille, which remain permanently closed.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbcearth.com/factfiles/animals/amphibians-reptiles/snake","d":"bbcearth.com","q":"To protect against scratches and debris, snakes have a brille, a thin, clear membrane-like scale that covers their eyes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Krokodiller kan ikke stikke tungen ud.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Krokodillers tunge er fastgjort, så den ikke kan stikkes ud.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their tongues are not free, but held in place by a membrane that limits movement; as a result, crocodiles are unable to stick out their tongues.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.niehs.nih.gov/health/kids/games/riddles/jokes/fun-facts-and-trivia","d":"niehs.nih.gov","q":"A crocodile cannot stick its tongue out.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En honningbi dør, når den har stukket.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Biens stik er med modhager, så den kan ikke trække det ud igen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey_bee","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The worker dies after the sting becomes lodged and is subsequently torn loose from the bee's abdomen.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/science/honeybee-sting-kill-bee","d":"pbs.org","q":"These blades are barbed in shape, and face outward like a harpoon.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En høne kan lægge æg uden en hane.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"Æggene er da ufrugtede.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://poultry.extension.org/articles/poultry-related-youth-programs/do-you-need-a-rooster-for-a-hen-to-lay-an-egg","d":"poultry.extension.org","q":"A hen (female chicken) does not need the help of a rooster (male chicken) in order to lay an egg.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/video/heres-why-humans-cant-lay-eggs-65dvwm/","d":"pbs.org","q":"But if the hen who laid this egg had mated with a rooster, that sperm would fertilize this ovum and grow","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Pingviner har en pigget tunge.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"Tungen hjælper med at holde på glat bytte.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A penguin has a spiny tongue and powerful jaws to grip slippery prey.","ok":true},{"u":"https://pbs.org/wnet/nature/the-world-of-penguins-deep-divers/1916","d":"pbs.org","q":"Their tongues are armed with sharp, backward-facing barbs that help prevent prey from escaping.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefants snabel har over 40.000 muskler.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"Snabelen er både næse, hånd og værktøj.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://kids.sandiegozoo.org/stories/noses-know","d":"kids.sandiegozoo.org","q":"And that long trunk has more than 40,000 muscles in it!","ok":true},{"u":"https://pbs.org/wgbh/nova/article/elephant-impressionists","d":"pbs.org","q":"an elephant trunk has over 40,000 muscles—more than all the muscles in a human body.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Guld kan spises.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Rent guld er giftfrit og bruges som pynt på mad.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Pure metallic (elemental) gold is non-toxic and non-irritating when ingested","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/39187-facts-about-gold.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"The gold isn't digested and just passes right through","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Honning fordærver aldrig.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Honning har næsten intet vand og kan holde sig i århundreder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"So long as its water concentration does not rise much above 18%, honey has an indefinite shelf life","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20250701-the-chemical-secrets-that-help-keep-honey-fresh-for-so-long","d":"bbc.com","q":"it will not go off","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Blæksprutteblod er blåt.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Blæksprutters blod er blåt, fordi det indeholder kobber.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"gives the blood a bluish colour","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.adfg.alaska.gov/index.cfm?adfg=giantpacificoctopus.printerfriendly","d":"adfg.alaska.gov","q":"having blue blood due to a copper-rich protein called hemocyanin","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Sommerfugle smager med fødderne.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Sommerfugle har smagssans i fødderne.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfly","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The long proboscis can be coiled when not in use for sipping nectar from flowers.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/55729998","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Butterflies taste with their feet!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Guldfisk har kun tre sekunders hukommelse.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Guldfisk kan huske i flere måneder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Goldfish have a memory span of at least three months","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/goldfish-memory.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"goldfish have such impressive memories","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hajer har ingen knogler.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Hajers skelet er lavet af brusk.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sharks and other cartilaginous fish (skates and rays) have skeletons made of cartilage and connective tissue.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/shark-facts","d":"livescience.com","q":"They do not have bones; their skeletons are made of a tissue called cartilage","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flok krager kaldes et mord.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"En gruppe krager kaldes et 'murder'.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-14","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crow","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The collective name for a group of crows is a \"murder\".","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/52716-crows-ravens.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"A murder of crows","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ko har ingen fortænder i overmunden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dentition","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The cow has no upper incisors or canines, the rostral portion of the upper jaw forming a dental pad.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Bos_taurus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Domestic cows have no upper incisors, instead they have a thick layer called the dental pad.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hval har bækkenben.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"notice the vestigial pelvis","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/beluga-whales.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"with only vestigial pelvic bones left unconnected to the spine.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En slange kan glide gennem luften.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"some arboreal species even capable of short-ranged gliding flight by flaring out the ribs","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/reptiles/facts/flying-snakes","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They're gliders, using the speed of free fall and contortions of their bodies to catch the air and generate lift.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En mus kan ikke kaste op.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_mouse","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"House mice, like most other rodents, can not vomit.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/28764-rodents-inability-to-vomit.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Rodents don't puke, and now researchers understand why.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et år på Venus er kortere end en dag på Venus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"a Venusian day is 116.75 Earth days long, about half a Venusian solar year, which is 224.7 Earth days long.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/venus/venus-facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"your “day” would be 243 Earth days long — longer even than a Venus year (one trip around the Sun), which takes only 225 Earth days.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Saturn er den eneste planet, der er lettere end vand.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Saturn is the only planet of the Solar System that is less dense than water—about 30% less.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/saturn/facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"It's hard to imagine, but Saturn is the only planet in our solar system with an average density that is less than water.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Strudser stikker hovedet i sandet, når de er bange.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Contrary to a popular assumption, ostriches do not bury their heads in sand to avoid danger.","ok":true},{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/ostrich","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"From far away, it looks like the ostrich has buried its head in the sand. Many people thought that was what ostriches did when they were trying to hide, but that is a myt","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kameler lagrer vand i deres pukler.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"It is a common myth that a camel stores water in its hump, but the humps in fact are reservoirs of fatty tissue, which can be used as a reserve source of calories, not wa","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/why-do-camels-have-humps.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Although camels do have tricks to make the most of water they find, their humps aren't one of them.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Svampe er planter.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fungus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In the past, mycology was regarded as a branch of botany, although it is now known that fungi are genetically more closely related to animals than to plants.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/53618-fungus.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Once thought simply to be plants, fungi have emerged as their own taxonomic kingdom.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hvaler er fisk.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Whales are a widely distributed and diverse group of fully aquatic placental marine mammals.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/animals/whales/whales-facts-about-the-largest-animals-on-earth","d":"livescience.com","q":"Whales are mammals — the same overall group that includes humans, dogs, cats, monkeys, pigs and others. Unlike fish, whales have lungs, not","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koalaer er bjørne.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"sometimes inaccurately called the koala bear, is an arboreal herbivorous marsupial native to Australia.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/33691-koalas-bears.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Though koalas are often called \"koala bears,\" they are not bears.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bananer vokser på træer.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scienceabc.com/pure-sciences/why-is-a-banana-tree-not-really-a-tree","d":"scienceabc.com","q":"A banana \"tree\" is not a tree at all. Botanically, the banana plant (genus Musa, family Musaceae) is a giant herbaceous monocot — essentially the world's largest herb.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Tomater er grøntsager.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomato","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The tomato is a plant whose fruit is an edible berry that is eaten as a vegetable.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/54615-tomato-nutrition.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"A botanist would tell you that a tomato is a fruit as well as a berry because it develops from a single fertilized ovary.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flagermus er blinde.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Microbats tend to have small eyes but are still sensitive to light, and no species is truly blind.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/55986-are-bats-really-blind.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Contrary to myth, bats aren't blind.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Guld kan spises.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Gold can be used in food and has the E number 175.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/39187-facts-about-gold.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Don't fear for your stomach: The gold isn't digested and just passes right through","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blæksprutte har tre hjerter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They have three hearts; a systemic or main heart that circulates blood around the body and two branchial or gill hearts that pump it through the two gills.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/55478-octopus-facts.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"An octopus has three hearts. The largest heart is called the systemic heart, The three-heart system is good at keeping blood pressure up.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koalaer har fingeraftryk ligesom mennesker.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/14007-koalas-human-fingerprints.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"koalas, doll-sized marsupials that climb trees with babies on their backs, have fingerprints that are almost identical to human ones.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/blog/tetrapod-zoology/vombatiform-radiation-part-i/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"Koalas famously possess human-like fingerprints","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Polarbjørnens hud er sort.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The polar bear is white or yellowish-furred with black skin and a thick layer of fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/43673-weird-facts-about-polar-bears.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Under their fur, polar bear skin is actually black.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Tungen har zoner for forskellige smage.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/7113-tongue-map-tasteless-myth-debunked.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"The notion that the tongue is mapped into four areas—sweet, sour, salty and bitter—is wrong.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scienceabc.com/eyeopeners/how-does-salt-enhance-the-flavor-of-food","d":"scienceabc.com","q":"The familiar grade-school “tongue map” that puts salt on the sides and sweetness on the tip is a misreading of that early data, not real biology.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Honning bliver aldrig dårlig.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/chemistry/does-honey-ever-go-bad","d":"livescience.com","q":"Raw honey — with intact enzymes and other beneficial compounds — is minimally processed and can last 'forever' if stored in a sealed container.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scienceabc.com/nature/does-honey-go-bad-expire-spoil","d":"scienceabc.com","q":"No, honey doesn’t go bad, spoil or expire on its own.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Der regner diamanter på Uranus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":14,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.space.com/diamond-rain-ice-giant-planets-uranus-neptune","d":"space.com","q":"Deep with frozen planets like Neptune and Uranus exotic diamond rains could occur more often than previously believed.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/whats-the-weirdest-planet-in-the-solar-system/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"On top of all that, it may also rain diamonds there","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Mennesker har kun fem sanser.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sense","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Although, in some cultures, five human senses were traditionally identified as such (namely sight, smell, touch, taste, and hearing), many more are now recognized.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/32314-how-many-senses-do-humans-have.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"But what we do perceive extends far beyond our everyday understanding of the five human senses: sight, smell, taste, hearing and touch.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hajer kan ikke få kræft.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/41655-great-white-shark-cancer.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"In total, scientists have now documented tumors in at least 23 species of sharks, including the two in the new study, Robbins said.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/sharks-do-get-cancer-tumor-found-great-white/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"In total, scientists have now documented tumors in at least 23 species of sharks, including the two in the new study, Robbins said.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kakerlakker kan overleve uden hoved i en uge.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockroach","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"While cockroaches do not have lungs as do vertebrates and can continue to respire if their heads are removed, in some very large species, the body musculature may contrac","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/fact-or-fiction-cockroach-can-live-without-head/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"cockroaches—and many other insects—can survive decapitation","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Giraffer har flere halsknogler end mennesker.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The long neck results from a disproportionate lengthening of the cervical vertebrae, not from the addition of more vertebrae.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/52407-how-giraffe-got-its-neck.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Giraffes, like humans, have seven cervical vertebrae, but the giraffe's vertebrae are large, measuring up to 10 inches (25.4 centimeters) long.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ko har en mave med fire kamre.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Koen har én mave med fire kamre: vom, netmave, bladmave og løbemave.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattle","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Cattle have one large stomach with four compartments; the rumen, reticulum, omasum, and abomasum.","ok":true},{"u":"https://beef.unl.edu/faq/basicquestions/","d":"beef.unl.edu","q":"Beef cattle are ruminants and ruminants have one large stomach with four compartments. Those compartments are the rumen, the reticulum, the omasum, and the abomasum.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Heste kan ikke kaste op.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Hestens spiserør møder maven i en skarp vinkel, så maden kun kan gå én vej.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Horses cannot vomit, so digestion problems can quickly cause colic, a leading cause of death.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bhs.org.uk/horse-care-and-welfare/health-care-management/horse-health/the-digestive-system/","d":"bhs.org.uk","q":"This sphincter is incredibly strong and is what prevents horses from being able to vomit.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Elefanter kan ikke hoppe.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"Elefanter kan kun gå eller løbe i en slags hurtig gang – aldrig hoppe.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Elephants are incapable of trotting, jumping, or galloping.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/african-elephant","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"But did you know elephants can't jump?","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kakerlakker kan være under vand i op til 40 minutter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"De lukker åbningerne i kroppen og holder vejret, mens de flyder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockroach","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"By doing this, cockroaches can remain submerged for up to 40 minutes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.pestworld.org/news-hub/pest-articles/fascinating-cockroach-facts","d":"pestworld.org","q":"A Cockroach Can Hold Its Breath for 40 Minutes","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hunde foretrækker at tisse med ryggen mod nord.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Når Jordens magnetfelt er roligt, vender de sig nord-syd.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Dogs prefer to defecate with their spines aligned in a north–south position in calm magnetic field conditions.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/42317-dogs-poop-along-north-south-magnetic-lines.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Dogs apparently prefer to poop while aligned with the north-south axis of the Earth's magnetic field.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kameleoner har en tunge, der er længere end deres krop.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Tungen kan skydes ud med lynets hast og gribe bytte på afstand.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"While the chameleons' tongues are typically thought to be one and a half to two times the length of their bodies","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wildlifemadagascar.org/animals/panther-chameleon","d":"wildlifemadagascar.org","q":"A panther chameleon’s tongue can stretch to 1.5 to 2 times its body length.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En slange har ingen øjenlåg.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Øjet er dækket af en gennemsigtig skæl, der beskytter det.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"they have eyelids, external ears and a fleshy non-forked tongue that snakes lack, although this rule is not universal.","ok":true},{"u":"https://phys.org/news/2022-06-snakes.html","d":"phys.org","q":"Because snakes don't have eyelids, they cannot blink","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Blæksprutter kan bruge værktøj.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"De samler kokosnøddeskaller og bruger dem som hus.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The veined octopus collects discarded coconut shells, then uses them to build a shelter, an example of tool use.","ok":true},{"u":"http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/mobile/science/nature/8408233.stm","d":"news.bbc.co.uk","q":"Writing in the journal Current Biology, the team says it is the first example of tool use in octopuses.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Snegle har tusindvis af tænder.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Tænderne sidder på en raspetunge, der skraber maden løs.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snail","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most snails have thousands of microscopic tooth-like structures located on a banded ribbon-like tongue called a radula.","ok":true},{"u":"https://nhm.org/stories/microscopic-look-snail-jaws","d":"nhm.org","q":"Snail teeth are called radula—thousands of microscopic spikes set on a flexible band.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ko har fire maver.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Koen har én mave med fire kamre, ikke fire separate maver.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattle","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Cattle have one large stomach with four compartments; the rumen, reticulum, omasum, and abomasum.","ok":true},{"u":"https://beef.unl.edu/faq/basicquestions/","d":"beef.unl.edu","q":"Beef cattle are ruminants and ruminants have one large stomach with four compartments. Those compartments are the rumen, the reticulum, the omasum, and the abomasum.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kameleoner kan ikke se farver.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"De ser både synligt lys og ultraviolet lys.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Chameleons can see in both visible and ultraviolet light.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/reptiles/facts/chameleons","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Chameleons can see a wide range of colors, from ultraviolet to infrared.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefant har tynd hud.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Elefanthuden er op til 2,5 cm tyk på ryggen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"An elephant's skin is generally very tough, at 2.5 cm (1 in) thick on the back and parts of the head.","ok":true},{"u":"https://tsavotrust.org/five-interesting-facts-about-an-elephants-skin","d":"tsavotrust.org","q":"With 2.5 cm thick skin, wrinkling and folding its way around a frame","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Pingviner kan flyve.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Pingviner er fugle, men deres vinger er svømmefødder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Penguins are a group of flightless semi-aquatic sea birds","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zkn2jsg","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Penguins are birds that live on the land and in the waters around the southern hemisphere. They cannot fly but are very good swimmers.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Delfiner sover med kun én hjernehalvdel ad gangen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Den anden hjernehalvdel holder øje med rovdyr og styrer vejrtrækningen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"one brain hemisphere in slow-wave sleep at a time","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/meet-the-animals-that-literally-sleep-with-one-eye-open/","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"one hemisphere of the animals' brain was in a state of slow-wave sleep, while the other was awake","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Myrer har ingen lunger.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"De trækker vejret gennem små huller i kroppen, kaldet spirakler.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Insects do not have lungs","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.howitworksdaily.com/how-do-ants-breathe","d":"howitworksdaily.com","q":"Ants, like all insects, don't have lungs","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Pingviner har knæ.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Knæet er skjult under fjerene, så man kun ser fødderne.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.scienceabc.com/eyeopeners/do-penguins-have-knees.html","d":"scienceabc.com","q":"penguins do have knees, and the joint is anatomically very similar to a mammalian (human) knee","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zt6rh4j","d":"bbc.co.uk","q":"Penguins' legs are made up of a femur, knee, fibula and tibia, much like a human's!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koalaer sover op til 20 timer om dagen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"De sparer energi, fordi eukalyptusblade giver lidt næring.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"sleep up to twenty hours a day","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/fascinating-facts/koala","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"They can sleep up to 18 hours a day","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Pingviner lever på Nordpolen.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Alle pingviner lever på den sydlige halvkugle.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"live almost exclusively in the Southern Hemisphere","ok":true},{"u":"https://polarguidebook.com/where-do-penguins-live","d":"polarguidebook.com","q":"Penguins live in the southern hemisphere.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hajer kan lugte en enkelt del blod i en million dele vand.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Det er en meget lille mængde, men ikke 'en dråbe i et olympisk bassin'.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"one part per million of blood in seawater","ok":true},{"u":"https://manoa.hawaii.edu/exploringourfluidearth/chemical/chemistry-and-seawater/elemental-abundance/weird-science-compare-your-sense-smell-shark-s-sense-smell","d":"manoa.hawaii.edu","q":"Sharks can smell blood from hundreds of meters away—in concentrations as low as one part per million (ppm).","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Edderkopper er insekter.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"Edderkopper er araknider og har otte ben, ikke seks.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"largest order of arachnids","ok":true},{"u":"https://tepapa.govt.nz/discover-collections/read-watch-play/science-and-nature/spiders-and-insects/your-bug-questions/what","d":"tepapa.govt.nz","q":"Arachnids have eight legs and no wings.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En slange kan høre musik.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Slanger kan mærke vibrationer, men ikke høre melodier.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"snakes lack external ears","ok":true},{"u":"https://snakeinformer.com/snakes-like-music","d":"snakeinformer.com","q":"Snakes don't enjoy music like people do.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bier har fem øjne.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"To store fasetøjne og tre små punktøjne på hovedet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-16","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"three small simple eyes (ocelli)","ok":true},{"u":"https://downloads.bbc.co.uk/breathingplaces/docs/beepart-nationaltrust.pdf","d":"downloads.bbc.co.uk","q":"Honey bees have five eyes!","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flodhest sveder blod.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Flodhestens røde 'sved' er hverken blod eller sved, men et naturligt solfilter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their skin secretes a natural, red-coloured sunscreen substance that is sometimes referred to as \"blood sweat\" but is neither blood nor sweat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/hippopotamus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"This reddish liquid is behind the myth that hippos sweat blood.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds har de største øjne af alle landdyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Et strudseøje måler ca. 5 cm i diameter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"their eyes are the largest of any land vertebrate, 50 mm (2.0 in) in diameter","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/amazing-eyes-vision-champions.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"An ostrich's eye is bigger than its brain, and is the largest eye of any living land animal, measuring five centimetres across.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En skovfrø kan fryse til is om vinteren og overleve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"Op til 70 % af vandet i kroppen bliver til is.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_frog","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"When frozen, wood frogs have no detectable vital signs: no heartbeat, breathing, blood circulation, muscle movement, or detectable brain activity.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/animals-freeze-then-thaw-explained","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The wood frog is one of the most frequently studied animals on Earth that freezes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flagermus er blinde.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"Alle flagermus kan se; nogle ser endda bedre end mennesker.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/are-bats-blind","d":"usgs.gov","q":"No, bats are not blind.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.batcon.org/blind-as-a-bat-no-such-thing","d":"batcon.org","q":"First things first - bats are NOT blind! Despite the common phrase, all bats have functional eyes and can see.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blækspruttes blod er blåt.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Blodet er blåt, fordi det transporterer ilt med kobberholdigt hæmocyanin i stedet for jernholdigt hæmoglobin.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"gives the blood a bluish colour","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/animal-blood-comes-in-a-rainbow-of-colors","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"octopuses have blue blood due to the oxygen-transporting protein hemocyanin","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda er en bjørn.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Den store panda tilhører bjørnefamilien (Ursidae).\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"is a bear species endemic to China","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ailuropoda_melanoleuca/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"giant pandas belong to the bear family","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala har to tommelfingre på hver hånd.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"De to første tæer på forpoten er modstående og fungerer som to tommelfingre, så koalaen kan gribe om grene.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"two opposable digits (the first and second, which are opposable to the other three)","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Phascolarctos_cinereus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"the first and second digits oppose the other three which enables the koala to grip branches","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En bi dør, efter den har stukket.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Arbejderbiens brod er modhage, så den river sig løs fra bierens krop og bier dør kort efter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee_sting","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Honey bees are the only bees to die after stinging","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Apis_mellifera/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"the sting and venom glands tear out of the abdomen, remaining embedded in the target. This causes the death of the worker","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En haj kan overleve i ferskvand.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Tyrehajen (bull shark) kan leve i både salt- og ferskvand og svømmer langt op i floder.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull_shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The bull shark is euryhaline and can thrive in both salt and fresh water","ok":true},{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/bull-shark","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"bull sharks have developed special adaptations that help them keep salt in their bodies even when they're in freshwater","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En pingvin kan holde vejret i 20 minutter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Kejserpingviner kan være under vand i omkring 20 minutter under jagt.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_penguin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the species can remain submerged around 20 minutes","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.facebook.com/WoodsHoleOcean/posts/-happy-worldpenguinday-did-you-know-that-emperor-penguins-can-dive-over-500-mete/819542523554594","d":"facebook.com","q":"They're known to hold their breath up to 20 minutes","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hval kan holde vejret i over 2 timer.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Cuviers næbhval har rekorden med dyk på over 2 timer og helt op til 3 timer og 42 minutter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuvier%27s_beaked_whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"making a dive that lasted 222 minutes (3.7 hours)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencenews.org/article/cuviers-beaked-whale-longest-record-dive","d":"sciencenews.org","q":"going 222 minutes, or three hours and 42 minutes, without coming up for air","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefant er bange for mus.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Det er en myte; elefanter reagerer på pludselig bevægelse, men er ikke bange for mus som sådan.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.livescience.com/33261-elephants-afraid-of-mice-.html","d":"livescience.com","q":"Elephants get a bit nervous sometimes when small, fast animals are around them","ok":true},{"u":"https://zooatlanta.org/busting-elephant-myths/","d":"zooatlanta.org","q":"There is no scientific evidence to suggests elephants are innately afraid of mice","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala drikker aldrig vand.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Koalaer får det meste vand fra eukalyptusblade, men kan godt drikke frit vand, især ved varme og tørke.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/fascinating-facts/koala","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"koalas rarely drink water as the majority of their water intake comes from eating fresh eucalyptus leaves","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/koala-bears-water-eucalyptus-leaves-trees-australia","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Koalas, which normally spend most of their time in the safety of eucalyptus trees, have begun to climb down and drink from artificial water stations","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hajer har ingen svømmeblære.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Hajer bruger en stor oliefyldt lever til opdrift i stedet for en svømmeblære.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"sharks do not have gas-filled swim bladders for buoyancy","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.whoi.edu/ocean-learning-hub/ocean-topics/ocean-life/sharks-other-fish/shark-facts/","d":"whoi.edu","q":"unlike most other fish, lack a swim bladder","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En pindsvin har omkring 5000 pigge.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Et voksent pindsvin har typisk 5000–7000 pigge af keratin.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/hedgehog","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"With about 3,000 to 5,000 quills covering its back","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.hedgehogstreet.org/about-hedgehogs/hedgehog-biology/","d":"hedgehogstreet.org","q":"An adult hedgehog has between 5,000 and 7,000 spines on it's body","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Den side af Månen, vi aldrig ser, er altid mørk.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Månens bagside får lige så meget sollys som forsiden; 'mørk' betyder 'usynlig', ikke 'uoplyst'.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/moon/top-moon-questions/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"There is no permanent dark side of the Moon. The far side of the Moon gets as much sunlight as the near side","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.space.com/42886-not-dark-side-of-moon-china-lunar-farside.html","d":"space.com","q":"Of course, there is a dark side of the moon... All that taken together means that any given point on the moon's surface spends about two weeks in light, then another two ","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Venus er den varmeste planet i solsystemet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Venus er varmere end Merkur, selv om Merkur er tættere på Solen, på grund af drivhuseffekt.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"making it the hottest planet in the solar system","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/venus/venus-facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"Venus is the hottest planet in our solar system","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et lyn er varmere end solens overflade.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Lyn kan opvarme luften til ca. 30.000 °C, omkring fem gange solens overfladetemperatur.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The air around the lightning flash rapidly heats to temperatures of about 30,000 °C (54,000 °F)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.weather.gov/safety/lightning-temperature","d":"weather.gov","q":"lightning can heat the air it passes through to 50,000 degrees Fahrenheit (5 times hotter than the surface of the sun)","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En kamel har tre øjenlåg.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Kameler har to ydre øjenlåg og et gennemsigtigt indre øjenlåg (nictiterende membran), der beskytter mod sand.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/camel","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"A thin nictitating membrane on each eye, like a clear inner eyelid, protects the eyes from sandstorms","ok":true},{"u":"https://kidsdiscover.com/did-you-know/camels-third-eyelid/","d":"kidsdiscover.com","q":"Camels have not one, not two, but three eyelids","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blåhval er det største dyr, der nogensinde har levet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Blåhvalen er større end nogen dinosaur og vejer op til ca. 200 tons.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.activewild.com/blue-whale","d":"activewild.com","q":"the blue whale (scientific name Balaenoptera musculus) holds the distinction of being the largest known animal ever to have lived on Earth","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.animalsaroundtheglobe.com/the-blue-whale-the-largest-animal-ever-known-to-have-lived-7-296552","d":"animalsaroundtheglobe.com","q":"the largest animal ever known to have existed in the history of life on Earth","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En delfin kan sove med ét øje åbent.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Delfiner sover med én hjernehalvdel ad gangen og holder det tilsvarende øje åbent.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"dolphins sleep with only one brain hemisphere in slow-wave sleep at a time","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/meet-the-animals-that-literally-sleep-with-one-eye-open","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"the animal's one open eye, linked to the contralateral awake hemisphere of the brain","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds kan løbe hurtigere end en hest.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"En struds sprinter ca. 70 km/t, mens en væddeløbshest kan nå ca. 71 km/t.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.schoolphysics.co.uk/age11-14/Mechanics/Motion/text/Animal_olympics/index.html","d":"schoolphysics.co.uk","q":"Horse (max) 71 44","ok":true},{"u":"https://nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/ostrich","d":"nationalzoo.si.edu","q":"they are the fastest two-legged animals on Earth","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Vand kan koge og fryse på samme tid.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Ved vands tripelpunkt (0,01 °C og 611 Pa) kan is, vand og damp eksistere samtidigt.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triple_point","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the unique combination of pressure and temperature at which liquid water, solid ice, and water vapour coexist in a stable equilibrium","ok":true},{"u":"https://physicstuff.com/thermodynamics/triple-point","d":"physicstuff.com","q":"the water reaches 273.16 K and 611.657 Pa — the triple point — and starts to freeze even as it keeps boiling","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En slange kan leve uden mad i et helt år.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Slanger har et meget langsomt stofskifte og kan faste i mange måneder, nogle op til et år.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"As an adaptation to these prolonged periods of fasting, they have lost the hunger hormone known as ghrelin","ok":true},{"u":"https://snake-identifier.app/blog/how-long-can-a-snake-go-without-eating","d":"snake-identifier.app","q":"some can fast for six months to a year or more without starving","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et menneske producerer nok spyt i løbet af livet til at fylde to svømmebassiner.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Med 1–2 liter spyt om dagen løber det op til omkring 25.000 liter i et liv.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://platinumpoolcare.com/item/1288-interesting-facts-about-swimming-and-swimming-pools","d":"platinumpoolcare.com","q":"The average human being produces 25,000 quarts of saliva, which is enough to fill up two whole swimming pools","ok":true},{"u":"https://beffadental.com/saliva-your-mouths-super-hero","d":"beffadental.com","q":"the average person will create enough saliva in their lifetime to fill two swimming pools","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En krokodille kan ikke række tungen ud.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Tungen sidder fast i ganen med en membran, så den ikke kan stikkes ud.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their tongues are not free, but held in place by a membrane that limits movement; as a result, crocodiles are unable to stick out their tongues","ok":true},{"u":"https://australian.museum/learn/animals/reptiles/estuarine-crocodile","d":"australian.museum","q":"Because the tongue and skull bones of a crocodile are not very movable","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefant er bange for mus.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fear_of_mice_and_rats","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"There is a common folklore belief that elephants are afraid of mice.","ok":true},{"u":"https://zooatlanta.org/busting-elephant-myths/","d":"zooatlanta.org","q":"There is no scientific evidence to suggests elephants are innately afraid of mice.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Mennesker har flere knogler som baby end som voksen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_skeleton","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The human skeleton is composed of around 270 bones at birth – this total decreases to around 206 bones by adulthood after some bones fuse together","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.healthline.com/health/how-many-bones-does-a-baby-have","d":"healthline.com","q":"Babies are born with around 300 bones, but some of these will fuse together with age. By adulthood, they’ll have just over 200 bones.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bier kan genkende menneskeansigter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vespula_vulgaris","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The species has been shown to be capable of recognizing human faces, a similar capacity as has been demonstrated for honey bees.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2009/01/090123101211.htm","d":"sciencedaily.com","q":"honeybees can learn to recognise human faces even when seen from different viewpoints.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bananer vokser på træer.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Banana plants are often mistaken for trees.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Gulerødder er altid orange.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrot","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Heirloom variants may be white, yellow, red, purple, or black.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrot","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"orange (crossbred), purple, white, red, or yellow root","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Is flyder på vand.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Because ice is less dense than liquid water, it floats","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"It floats on water because ice has less density than water.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En kolibri kan flyve baglæns.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummingbird","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"enabling helicopter-like flight in any direction, including the ability to hover.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hummingbird","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They are also the only group of birds able to fly backwards.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hunde kan ikke svede.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermoregulation","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Mammals like cats, dogs, and pigs rely on panting or other means for thermal regulation and have sweat glands only in their foot pads and snouts.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.akc.org/expert-advice/health/do-dogs-sweat/","d":"akc.org","q":"dogs sweat through their paws","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flamingoer er født lyserøde.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Young flamingos hatch with greyish-red plumage","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Baby flamingos are gray.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blæksprutte kan skifte farve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Octopuses use camouflage to hunt and to avoid predators. To do this, they use specialised skin cells that change colour.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"use colour-changing camouflage.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koalaer spiser kun eukalyptusblade.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Koalas typically inhabit open Eucalyptus woodland, as the leaves of these trees make up most of their diet.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They eat leaves of eucalyptus trees.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefants snabel er dens næse.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Distinctive features of elephants include a long proboscis called a trunk","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"The trunk is a very long nose, made from the upper lip.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Lyden rejser hurtigere i vand end i luft.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwater_environment","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sound is transmitted about 4.3 times faster in water (1,484 m/s in fresh water) than in air (343 m/s).","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Sound can travel through water faster than through air","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En øgle kan kaste halen af.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizard","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Many lizards, including geckos and skinks, are capable of shedding their tails (autotomy).","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizard","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They can also sacrifice and regrow their tails.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hval kan være større end et hus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Reaching a maximum confirmed length of 29.9–30.5 m (98–100 ft) and weighing up to 190–200 t","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_whale","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"This makes blue whales the largest animals to ever live on Earth","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bananer er botanisk set et bær.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"They are considered to be berries.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds er den hurtigste fugl på land.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With the ability to run at 70 km/h (43 mph), they are the fastest birds on land.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Ostriches do not fly, but can run faster than any other bird.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds har de største øjne af alle landdyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird_vision","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The ostrich has the largest eye of any land vertebrate","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Ostriches have the biggest eyes of all land animals.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flue kan se i næsten alle retninger.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compound_eye","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Compared with single-aperture eyes, compound eyes have poor image resolution; however, they possess a very large view angle","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Also flies have large eyes with excellent wide-angle vision.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds kan ikke flyve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Ostriches are large flightless birds.","ok":true},{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrich","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"Ostriches do not fly","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bananer er bær.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/banan","d":"lex.dk","q":"Frugten er et bær med læderagtig ydre væg","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Tomater er frugter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/tomat","d":"lex.dk","q":"Frugten er et saftigt, to- eller flerrummet, oftest kuglerundt bær","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomato","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"is a plant whose fruit is an edible berry","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Peanuts er nødder.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/jordnød","d":"lex.dk","q":"Frugten er en uopspringende bælg med 2-3 meget olierige frø.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Botanically they are not nuts","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Jordnødder vokser under jorden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/jordnød","d":"lex.dk","q":"Nederst på stænglen og under jorden dannes små, selvbestøvende blomster.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Peanut fruits develop underground","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Vanilje kommer fra en orkidé.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":5,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://lex.dk/vanilje","d":"lex.dk","q":"Vanilje er en slægt af klatrende, tropiske orkidéer.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Vanilla is a spice derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Kanel kommer fra træbark.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":4,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf",