constantly throughout life.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En slange kan sluge et bytte, der er større end dens hoved.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Slanger har løse kæber, så de kan sluge store bytte.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"For example, the African egg-eating snake has flexible jaws adapted for eating eggs much larger than the diameter of its head.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/reptiles/facts/snakes-1","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Snakes eat all sorts of animals, from small mammals and small fish to larger prey up to three times larger than the width of their head.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En afskåret blækspruttearm kan stadig bevæge sig.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Blækspruttens arme har egne nervecentre og kan reagere uden hjernen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octopus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A severed arm can still move and respond to stimuli.","ok":true},{"u":"https://scientificamerican.com/blog/octopus-chronicles/why-don-t-octopuses-get-stuck-to-themselves","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"a severed octopus arm can respond to stimuli and even activate its suckers for more than an hour.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Nogle slanger kan se infrarødt.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Pitviper har varmefølsomme organer, der opfanger infrarødt lys.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pit_viper","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"These loreal pits are the external openings to a pair of extremely sensitive infrared-detecting organs, which","ok":true},{"u":"https://scientificamerican.com/article/snakes-flexible-heat-sensing-organs-explained","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"Pit vipers like this one have extremely sensitive heat vision.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blæksprutte kan skifte farve, mens den sover.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Blæksprutter skifter farve under søvnens aktive fase.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cephalopod","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The octopus changes skin color and texture during quiet and active sleep cycles.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.npr.org/2021/03/25/980944495/sleeping-octopuses-may-have-dreams-but-theyre-probably-brief","d":"npr.org","q":"they were brief but obvious; the octopuses' skin darkened and their bodies and suckers contracted.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda bruger det meste af dagen på at spise bambus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Pandaer spiser bambus i mange timer, fordi bambus giver lidt energi.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"A typical animal eats half the day—a full 12 out of every 24 hours—and relieves itself dozens of times a day.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/wildlife/giant-pandas","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"Giant pandas spend 10-16 hours a day feeding, mainly on bamboo.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En kakerlak kan overleve en atombombe.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Kakerlakker er mere strålingsfølsomme end myterne siger.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockroach","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"An urban legend maintains that cockroaches are radiation-resistant, and thus would survive a nuclear war.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencefocus.com/nature/is-it-true-that-cockroaches-could-survive-a-nuclear-holocaust","d":"sciencefocus.com","q":"a cockroach can only survive between six and 15 times the lethal radiation dose for humans.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flodhest kan løbe hurtigere end et menneske.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Flodheste kan løbe op til 30 km/t på land.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Hippos are reported to reach 30 km/h (19 mph) but this has not been confirmed.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/hippopotamus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"22 miles per hour on land over short distances.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flodhest er tungere end en elefant.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Elefanten er det tyngste landdyr; flodhesten er mindre.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","d":"simple.wikipedia.org","q":"elephant is the heaviest and the white rhinoceros is the second heaviest","ok":true},{"u":"https://scientificamerican.com/article/highly-mobile-testicles-frustrate-effort-to-calm-hippos-in-captivity","d":"scientificamerican.com","q":"The hippopotamus is among the world’s largest creatures on land. Only elephants and some species of rhino are larger.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hvalhaj er en hval.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Hvalhajen er en fisk (en haj), ikke et pattedyr.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale_shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The name \"whale shark\" refers to the animal's appearance and large size; it is a fish, not a mammal, and, like all sharks, is not closely related to whales.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.wwf.org.uk/learn/fascinating-facts/whale-sharks","d":"wwf.org.uk","q":"Although these huge sea creatures are called ‘whale sharks’, they are not actually whales, but filter-feeding sharks","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds kan sparke hårdt nok til at dræbe en løve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Strudsen forsvarer sig med kraftige spark.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/ostrich","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Ostrich kicks can kill a human or a potential predator like a lion.","ok":true},{"u":"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/ostrich","d":"kids.nationalgeographic.com","q":"An ostrich will kick with a force mighty enough to kill a lion.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hvalhaj har tusindvis af små tænder.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Hvalhajens mange tænder er små og bruges ikke til at tygge.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.pbs.org/wnet/nature/blog/whale-shark-fact-sheet","d":"pbs.org","q":"Whale sharks have thousands of tiny teeth that they can only shrimp fish and plankton by using its modified gill rakers as a suction filter.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Rhincodon_typus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"containing up to 300 rows of hundreds of tiny, hooked, and replaceable teeth.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blåhvals sang kan høres over 1000 km væk.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Blåhvalens lave kald kan rejse tusindvis af kilometer i havet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20230815-how-undersea-sounds-help-us-understand-ocean-life","d":"bbc.com","q":"travelling for thousands of kilometres","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/news/2022/july/underwater-noise-pollution-risking-lives-whales-dolphins.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"can produce calls that can be heard hundreds or even thousands of kilometres from the whale which made them.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En struds har de største øjne af alle landdyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Et strudseøje måler omkring 5 cm i diameter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_ostrich","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"their eyes are the largest of any land vertebrate, 50 mm (2.0 in) in diameter","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/amazing-eyes-vision-champions.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"They also have the largest eyes of any living land animal.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En girafs tunge er over 40 cm lang.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Giraffens tunge er lang og kan nå de høje blade.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"A giraffe's tongue is about 45 cm (18 in) long.","ok":true},{"u":"https://giraffeconservation.org/facts-about-giraffe/how-long-is-a-giraffes-tongue-what-color-is-it/","d":"giraffeconservation.org","q":"45 to 50 centimeters (or 17 to 19 inches) long","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et pindsvin har en vis modstandskraft mod slangegift.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Pindsvinet har proteiner, der delvis neutraliserer slangegift.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedgehog","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Like opossums, mice, and moles, hedgehogs have some natural immunity against some snake venom through the protein erinacin in their muscles, though in such small amounts ","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nhm.ac.uk/discover/bite-or-be-bitten.html","d":"nhm.ac.uk","q":"So far scientists fully understand venom resistance in only four mammals - mongooses, honey badgers, hedgehogs and pigs - as well as several snakes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Den mindste kolibri vejer under 2 gram.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Den mindste fugl i verden, bi-kolibrien, vejer under 2 gram.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee_hummingbird","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"1.95 g (0.069 oz)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.audubon.org/magazine/get-know-bee-hummingbird-worlds-smallest-bird","d":"audubon.org","q":"They weigh less than two grams — less than a dime.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et menneske kan svømme gennem en blåhvals hovedpulsåre.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Blåhvalens hovedpulsåre er kun stor nok til et menneskehoved, ikke hele kroppen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://blog.education.nationalgeographic.com/2015/08/31/how-big-is-a-blue-whales-heart","d":"blog.education.nationalgeographic.com","q":"people could swim through their aortas","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/sciencetech/article-3206564/See-worlds-biggest-heart-Incredible-5ft-long-organ-blue-whale-revealed-scientists-time.html","d":"dailymail.co.uk","q":"The aorta – the heart's main artery – wasn't big enough to fit a whole human inside, but could fit a human head, the researchers said.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Havodder flyder på ryggen, når de sover.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_otter","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"When at the surface, it usually floats on its back and moves by sculling its feet and tail from side to side.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/sea-otter","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They sleep this way, often gathered in groups.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En næsehornshorn er lavet af keratin (det samme som hår og negle).\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoceros","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same material as hair and fingernails","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/rhinoceros","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"A rhino’s horn is made of keratin, the same material that makes up our fingernails and hair.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Katte kan ikke smage sødt.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Domestic and wild cats share a taste receptor gene mutation that keeps their sweet taste buds from binding to sugary molecules, leaving them with no ability to taste swee","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/domestic-cat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Domestic cats lack a taste receptor for sweetness.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hunds lugtesans er 10.000 til 100.000 gange bedre end menneskers.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Dogs have roughly forty times more smell-sensitive receptors than humans, ranging from about 125 million to nearly 300 million in some dog breeds, such as bloodhounds.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/domestic-dog","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"the domestic dog’s sense of smell is between 10,000 and 100,000 better than our own","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda har en 'tommelfinger', der er en knogle i håndleddet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The giant panda's paw has a digit similar to a thumb and five fingers; the thumb-like digit is actually a modified sesamoid bone that helps it to hold bamboo while eating","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"it hungrily plucks the stalks with elongated wrist bones that function rather like thumbs.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En zebras striber er unikke – ingen to zebraer har samme mønster.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zebra","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Zebra stripes come in different patterns, unique to each individual.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/zebra","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Each animal's stripes are as unique as fingerprints—no two are exactly alike","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flodhest 'sveder' rødt – en naturlig solcreme.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Their skin secretes a natural, red-coloured sunscreen substance that is sometimes referred to as 'blood sweat' but is neither blood nor sweat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/hippopotamus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"When basking on the shore, they secrete an oily red sweat-like substance that moistens their skin, repels water, and protects them from the sun and germs.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En mantisreje kan se flere farver end mennesker.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":11,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis_shrimp","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Compared with the four types of photoreceptor cell that humans possess in their eyes, the eyes of a mantis shrimp have between 12 and 16 types of photoreceptor cells.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/invertebrates/facts/mantis-shrimp","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Human eyes have three photoreceptors—cells that detect color—to distinguish between blue, green, and red light. With a staggering 12 photoreceptors, mantis shrimp can see","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En manet har hverken hjerne eller hjerte.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jellyfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most jellyfish do not have specialized systems for osmoregulation, respiration and circulation, and do not have a central nervous system.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/invertebrates/facts/box-jellyfish","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"without a central nervous system, scientists aren’t sure how they process what they see.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan dreje hovedet 270 grader.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Owls can rotate their heads and necks as much as 270°.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"they make up for their lack of ocular musculature with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan ikke bevæge øjnene – den drejer hovedet i stedet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"they must rotate their entire heads to change the focus of their view because, like most birds, their eyes are fixed in their sockets.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Although they can’t move their large eyes, they make up for their lack of ocular musculature with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En vombats pung vender bagud.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wombat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"One distinctive adaptation of wombats is their backward pouch.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/wombat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Unlike other marsupials such as kangaroos and koalas, the opening of a wombat’s pouch faces her rear rather than her head to prevent it filling with dirt when the mother ","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Næbdyr er et pattedyr, der lægger æg.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platypus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The platypus (Ornithorhynchus anatinus), sometimes referred to as the duck-billed platypus, is a semiaquatic, egg-laying mammal endemic to eastern Australia","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/platypus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"It is one of only two mammals (the echidna is the other) that lay eggs.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Søhesthanner bærer ungerne.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seahorse","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The male seahorse is equipped with a brood pouch on the ventral, or front-facing, side of the tail. When mating, the female seahorse deposits up to 1,500 eggs in the male","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/seahorse","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"In a reproductive role reversal unique to seahorses and others in the family Syngnathidae (which also includes pipefish and sea dragons), males experience pregnancy.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blåhval har det største hjerte af alle dyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The weight of the heart of a stranded North Atlantic blue whale was 180 kg (400 lb), the largest known in any animal.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Their hearts, as much as an automobile.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En gepard er det hurtigste landdyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheetah","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The cheetah is a pursuit predator and the fastest land animal, capable of running at 93–104 km/h (58–65 mph)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/cheetah","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The cheetah is the world's fastest land mammal.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En elefanttrunk består af op til 150.000 muskelbundter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":10,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"This versatile appendage contains up to 150,000 separate muscle fascicles, with no bone and little fat.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/elephant","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"There are eight major muscles on each side of the trunk and 150,000 muscle fascicles (portions of muscles) throughout the entire trunk.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Flodheste kan ikke svømme – de går på bunden.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"They move in the water by walking or bouncing off the bottom, rarely entering deep water.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/hippopotamus","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Hippos cannot swim or breathe underwater","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En giraf har 7 halspattedyr – præcis som mennesker.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giraffe","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"exceptions to the mammalian limit of seven cervical vertebrae","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/giraffe","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"How many bones are there in a giraffe's neck? Just like humans, giraffes have seven neck vertebrae.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En tigers striber er unikke for hvert enkelt dyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":9,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"distinctive black or dark brown stripes, which are uniquely patterned in each individual.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/tiger","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"Each tiger has its very own stripe pattern. Conservation scientists who study tigers can identify individuals by their unique stripes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En edderkop er et insekt.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Unlike insects, spiders do not have antennae.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/invertebrates/facts/spiders","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Spiders are arachnids, a class of arthropods that also includes scorpions, mites, and ticks.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan dreje hovedet helt rundt.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Owls can rotate their heads and necks as much as 270°.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"they make up for their lack of ocular musculature with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan flyve lydløst.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most owls share an innate ability to fly almost silently and also more slowly in comparison to other birds of prey.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Because the edges of owl feathers are soft instead of stiff, the carnivores have an advantage over their targets: a silent swoop.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flagermus sover om dagen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most bats are nocturnal, and many roost in caves or other refuges;","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/bats","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They spend their daylight hours hiding in roosts around the tropics, dense forests, and wetlands.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hval er en fisk.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Whales are a widely distributed and diverse group of fully aquatic placental marine mammals.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Blue whales are the largest animals ever known to have lived on Earth. These magnificent marine mammals rule the oceans at up to 100 feet long and upwards of 200 tons.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En haj er et pattedyr.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sharks are a group of elasmobranch cartilaginous fishes","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/sharks","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Like rays and skates, sharks fall into a subclass of fish called elasmobranchii.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala er en bjørn.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The koala (Phascolarctos cinereus), sometimes inaccurately called the koala bear, is an arboreal herbivorous marsupial native to Australia.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/koala","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Often called the koala 'bear,' this tree-climbing animal is a marsupial—a mammal with a pouch for the development of offspring.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En manet har hverken hjerne eller hjerte.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jellyfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Most jellyfish do not have specialized systems for osmoregulation, respiration and circulation, and do not have a central nervous system.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/uk/discover/animals/sea-life/jellyfish-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"Jellyfish have no brain, heart, bones or eyes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En manet er en fisk.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jellyfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Jellyfish, also known as sea jellies or simply jellies, are the medusa-phase of certain gelatinous members of the subphylum Medusozoa, which is a major part of the phylum","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/uk/discover/animals/sea-life/jellyfish-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"Classification: Invertebrate","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En blåhval er det største dyr, der nogensinde har levet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the blue whale, which is the largest known animal that has ever lived.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Blue whales are the largest animals ever known to have lived on Earth.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hajs skelet er lavet af brusk.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sharks are a group of elasmobranch cartilaginous fishes","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/sharks","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Species in this subclass have skeletons made from cartilage, not bone, and have five to seven gill slits on each side of their heads","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala er et pungdyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The koala (Phascolarctos cinereus), sometimes inaccurately called the koala bear, is an arboreal herbivorous marsupial native to Australia.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/koala","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"this tree-climbing animal is a marsupial—a mammal with a pouch for the development of offspring.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En ugle kan bevæge øjnene.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"they must rotate their entire heads to change the focus of their view because, like most birds, their eyes are fixed in their sockets.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/birds/facts/owl","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Although they can’t move their large eyes, they make up for their lack of ocular musculature with necks that can twist up to 270 degrees to track the movement of prey.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda spiser bambus.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Despite its taxonomic classification as a carnivoran, the giant panda's diet is primarily herbivorous, with approximately 99% of its diet consisting of bamboo.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"The giant panda has an insatiable appetite for bamboo.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda spiser kun bambus.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Despite its taxonomic classification as a carnivoran, the giant panda's diet is primarily herbivorous, with approximately 99% of its diet consisting of bamboo.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Pandas will sometimes eat birds or rodents as well.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En panda spiser nogle gange kød.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Despite its taxonomic classification as a carnivoran, the giant panda's diet is primarily herbivorous, with approximately 99% of its diet consisting of bamboo.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/giant-panda","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Pandas will sometimes eat birds or rodents as well.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En koala drikker ikke meget vand.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The koala replaces lost water at a lower rate than species such as some possums.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/koala","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Koalas usually don’t drink much water as they get most of their moisture from these leaves.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flagermus kan flyve.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Bats are more agile in flight than most birds, using long, spread-out digits covered with a thin membrane or patagium.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/bats","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They are the only mammals in the world that can fly, and they are remarkably good at it.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En manet har ingen knogler.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":8,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jellyfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Jellyfish, also known as sea jellies or simply jellies, are the medusa-phase of certain gelatinous members of the subphylum Medusozoa, which is a major part of the phylum","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.natgeokids.com/uk/discover/animals/sea-life/jellyfish-facts/","d":"natgeokids.com","q":"Jellyfish have no brain, heart, bones or eyes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En hval er et pattedyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":6,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Whales are a widely distributed and diverse group of fully aquatic placental marine mammals.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/blue-whale","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Blue whales are the largest animals ever known to have lived on Earth. These magnificent marine mammals rule the oceans at up to 100 feet long and upwards of 200 tons.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En flagermus er et pattedyr.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":7,\"e\":\"\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Bats (order Chiroptera) are winged mammals, the only mammals capable of true and sustained flight.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/bats","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"For centuries, bats have been called sinister and spooky, likely because of their beady eyes and razor-sharp fangs.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Nogle papegøjefisk sover indpakket i en slimkugle, som de selv har lavet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Slimen menes at skjule fiskens lugt for rovdyr.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parrotfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Some parrotfish species, such as the queen parrotfish (Scarus vetula), secrete a mucus cocoon, particularly at night","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/parrotfish","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Every night, certain species of parrotfish envelope themselves in a transparent cocoon made of mucous secreted from an organ on their head.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En havboksmanet har kun to øjne.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Den har 24 øjne: seks i hver af fire klynger.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box_jellyfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In total, the box jellyfish have six eyes on each of their four rhopalia, creating a total of 24 eyes.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/invertebrates/facts/box-jellyfish","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"They also have eyes grouped in clusters of six on the four sides of their bell.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hos nogle tudsefisk smelter hannen sammen med hunnen og lever resten af livet som en parasit på hende.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":14,\"e\":\"Hannen er meget mindre end hunnen og får føde fra hende.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglerfish","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"where the male attaches to the much larger female, sometimes fusing together as an example of natural parabiosis","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/fish/facts/anglerfish","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"it has evolved into a permanent parasitic mate","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"En nøgenrotte kan overleve 18 minutter uden ilt.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Den mister bevidstheden og sænker pulsen kraftigt.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naked_mole_rat","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In zero-oxygen atmosphere, it can survive 18 minutes apparently without suffering any harm","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/facts/naked-mole-rat","d":"nationalgeographic.com","q":"Can Survive 18 Minutes Without Oxygen","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hornøgler sprøjter vand ud af øjnene for at skræmme rovdyr.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Det er blod, ikke vand – det kan sprøjte op til cirka halvanden meter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_lizard","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"are also able to squirt an aimed stream of blood from the corners of the eyes for a distance up to 5 ft (1.5 m)","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.nps.gov/grca/learn/nature/short-horned-lizard.htm","d":"nps.gov","q":"When threatened, short-horned lizards shoot blood from specialized tear ducts in the corners of their eyes.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et tretået dovendyr kommer ned på jorden for at gå på toilettet cirka en gang om ugen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Det kommer ned fra træerne for at grave afføringen ned.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloth","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Sloths descend about once every eight days to defecate on the ground.","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/dovendyr","d":"lex.dk","q":"Tretåede dovendyr gør det ca. en gang om ugen","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Næbdyret har ikke dievorter, så mælken siver ud gennem huden på maven.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Ungerne slikker mælken af pelsen.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platypus","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With no teats, the milk is released through pores in the skin from which the young lap it up in her fur.","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/n%C3%A6bdyr","d":"lex.dk","q":"Kirtlerne udskiller mælk over huden, så ungerne kan slikke den i sig.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Koraldyr er dyr og ikke planter.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Koraldyr sidder fast og fanger føde med fangarme.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria.","ok":true},{"u":"https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/coral.html","d":"oceanservice.noaa.gov","q":"Coral, a sessile animal, relies on its relationship with plant-like algae to build the largest structures of biological origin on Earth","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Hundredårskrigen varede præcis 100 år.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Den varede fra 1337 til 1453 – altså 116 år.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hundred_Years%27_War","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Medieval Anglo-French conflicts, 1337–1453","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/Hundred%C3%A5rskrigen","d":"lex.dk","q":"Hundredårskrigen var krige mellem England og Frankrig 1337-1453.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Nintendo blev grundlagt i 1889 og solgte oprindeligt japanske spillekort.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Videospillene kom først mange år senere.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The history of Nintendo began when craftsman Fusajiro Yamauchi founded the company in 1889 to produce handmade hanafuda playing cards.","ok":true},{"u":"https://snl.no/Nintendo","d":"snl.no","q":"Nintendo ble etablert i 1889 og produserte opprinnelig japanske spillkort.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Mikrobølgeovnens opfindelse startede med et uheld, hvor en ingeniørs chokoladebar smeltede i lommen.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Percy Spencer arbejdede med radar, da chokoladen smeltede.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microwave_oven","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"he noticed that microwaves from an active radar set he was working on started to melt a candy bar he had in his pocket.","ok":true},{"u":"https://snl.no/mikrob%C3%B8lgeovn","d":"snl.no","q":"Han oppdaget at en sjokoladeplate i lommen hans smeltet som følge av mikrobølgene.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Teflon blev opdaget ved et uheld i 1938.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Roy Plunkett ledte efter et nyt kølemiddel.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teflon","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) was accidentally discovered in 1938 by Roy J. Plunkett","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.sciencehistory.org/education/scientific-biographies/roy-j-plunkett/","d":"sciencehistory.org","q":"Teflon, discovered by Roy J. Plunkett (1910–1994) at the DuPont Company’s Jackson Laboratory in 1938, was an accidental invention","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Bobleplast blev oprindeligt opfundet som et slags tapet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Tapetet blev en fiasko, men plasten blev god emballage.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubble_wrap","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In 1957, two inventors named Alfred Fielding and Marc Chavannes were attempting to create a three-dimensional plastic wallpaper.","ok":true},{"u":"https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/01/25/celebrating-half-a-century-of-loud-soothing-pops/","d":"cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com","q":"had been created a textured plastic wallpaper in 1957","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Tyggegummi blev oprindeligt lavet af saften fra et træ.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Stoffet chicle kommer fra sapodillatræet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chewing_gum","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"they used chicle, a natural tree gum, as a base for making a gum-like substance","ok":true},{"u":"https://snl.no/tyggegummi","d":"snl.no","q":"Man begynte etter hvert å lage tyggegummi fremstilt av chicle, en naturlig plantegummi fra sapodilletreet.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Superlim blev opdaget ved et uheld, da forskere ledte efter noget helt andet.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Forskerne ledte efter klart plastik til våbensigter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyanoacrylate","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In 1942, a team of scientists headed by Harry Coover Jr. stumbled upon a formulation that stuck to everything with which it came in contact.","ok":true},{"u":"https://snl.no/superlim","d":"snl.no","q":"Superlim ble oppdaget ved en tilfeldighet i 1951 av kjemikeren Harry Coover","ok":true}]},"k