ipedia.org/wiki/Great_Red_Spot","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Measuring 16,350 km (10,160 mi) in width as of 3 April 2017, the Great Red Spot is 1.3 times the diameter of Earth.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"Jupiter’s iconic Great Red Spot is a giant storm bigger than Earth that has raged for hundreds of years.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Et døgn på Mars varer over 30 timer.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Et døgn på Mars varer cirka 24 timer og 40 minutter.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The solar day (or sol) on Mars is only slightly longer than an Earth day: 24 hours, 39 minutes, and 35.244 seconds.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/mars/facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"it completes one rotation every 24.6 hours, which is very similar to one day on Earth (23.9 hours).","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Jupiters måne Io har hundredvis af vulkaner.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Io er det mest vulkansk aktive sted i solsystemet.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Io_(moon)","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"With over 400 active volcanoes, Io is the most geologically active object in the Solar System.","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/moons/io/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"Io is the most volcanically active world in the solar system, with hundreds of volcanoes","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Under isen på Jupiters måne Europa findes der et stort saltvandshav.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"Forskere mener, at havet kan rumme liv.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Europa_(moon)","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The apparent youth and smoothness of the surface is due to a water ocean beneath the surface","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/moons/europa/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"There is strong evidence Jupiter's moon Europa has a saltwater ocean","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Saturns ringe består mest af sten.\",\"t\":false,\"age\":13,\"e\":\"De består næsten udelukkende af vandis med lidt støv og sten.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rings_of_Saturn","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"are made almost entirely of water ice, with a trace component of rocky material","ok":true},{"u":"https://science.nasa.gov/saturn/facts/","d":"science.nasa.gov","q":"They are made of billions of small chunks of ice and rock","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"Tivolis rutsjebane er bygget af træ og stammer fra 1914.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Den er en af verdens ældste træ-rutsjebaner, der stadig kører.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli_Gardens","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The park is best known for its wooden roller coaster, Rutschebanen, or as some people call it, Bjergbanen (The Mountain Coaster), built in 1914.","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/Tivoli","d":"lex.dk","q":"Tivolis 720 m lange rutsjebane af træ fra 1914 er verdens ældste, stadig fungerende rutsjebane.","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"I Rundetårn kommer man op ad en snoet gang i stedet for trapper.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":12,\"e\":\"Gangen snor sig flere gange rundt om tårnets kerne.\"}":{"pool":"ktf","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-18","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rundetaarn","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Instead of stairs, a 7.5-turn spiral ramp forms the only access way to the towertop observatory","ok":true},{"u":"https://lex.dk/Rundet%C3%A5rn","d":"lex.dk","q":"Man træder lige ind i Sneglegangen, som er en trinløs murstensbeklædt lang gang","ok":true}]},"ktf|{\"s\":\"På Saturns måne Titan findes der søer af flydende metan.\",\"t\":true,\"age\":