tatus":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Oddity","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"It was released on 11 July 1969 by Philips and Mercury Records as a 7-inch single","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.udiscovermusic.com/artists/david-bowie/","d":"udiscovermusic.com","q":"A more established sound and vision emerged with the space-age hit 'Space Oddity', which earned Bowie his first Top 5 chart placing when it was released in 1969.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilket berømt rockband optrådte under navnet «The High Numbers», før det vendte tilbage til sit eget navn?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Who","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"He renamed the group the High Numbers, dressed them up in mod clothes","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.udiscovermusic.com/artists/the-who/","d":"udiscovermusic.com","q":"They also acquired a manager, Peter Meaden who decided that the Who was a terrible name and decided they should be called The High Numbers","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilket band blev dannet af Jimmy Page i 1968 under navnet «The New Yardbirds»?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Led_Zeppelin","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Led Zeppelin evolved from a previous band, the Yardbirds, and were originally named \"the New Yardbirds\".","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.udiscovermusic.com/artists/led-zeppelin/","d":"udiscovermusic.com","q":"Still called The New Yardbirds when sessions commenced for their eponymous debut, Led Zeppelin laid down a marker.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken sang skrev Henry Mancini og Johnny Mercer til filmen «Breakfast at Tiffany's» fra 1961?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_River","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Moon River is a song composed by Henry Mancini with lyrics by Johnny Mercer. It was originally performed by Audrey Hepburn in the 1961 film Breakfast at Tiffany's, winnin","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/the-meaning-behind-andy-williams-moon-river/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"Moon River was originally written by composer Henry Mancini and lyricist Johnny Mercer for the 1961 film, Breakfast at Tiffany's.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken 1966-sang skrev Neil Diamond, og The Monkees gjorde den til et kæmpehit?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I%27m_a_Believer","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"I'm a Believer is a song written by Neil Diamond and recorded by the American pop rock band the Monkees in 1966 with the lead vocals by Micky Dolenz.","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/these-3-songs-were-written-by-neil-diamond-but-became-big-hits-for-other-artists/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"Diamond is the sole writer of The Monkees' I'm a Believer.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken Beatles-sang havde arbejdstitlen «Scrambled Eggs»?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yesterday_(Beatles_song)","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The working title was \"Scrambled Eggs\".","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/3-iconic-beatles-songs-that-had-weird-working-titles/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"The working title for this Lennon-McCartney collaboration was Scrambled Eggs.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilket band tog navn efter en bog af filosoffen Aldous Huxley?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Doors","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The band took its name from the title of the English writer Aldous Huxley's book The Doors of Perception","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/behind-the-band-name-the-doors/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"The Doors took its name from the autobiographical book, The Doors of Perception, by English writer and philosopher Aldous Huxley.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken gammel folkemelodi gjorde The Animals til et verdenshit i 1964?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_House_of_the_Rising_Sun","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The House of the Rising Sun is an American traditional folk song, sometimes called Rising Sun Blues.","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/this-1964-folk-standard-turned-pop-hit-was-originally-an-attempt-to-stand-out-at-chuck-berry-concerts/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"House Of The Rising Sun, a traditional folk tune that, in its most recognizable forms, dates back to the early 1900s.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken 1965-sang af The Byrds låner teksten fra Prædikerens Bog i Bibelen?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turn!_Turn!_Turn!","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The lyrics – except for the title, which is repeated throughout the song, and the final two lines – consist of the first eight verses of the third chapter of the biblical","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/before-turn-turn-turn-the-byrds-were-about-to-cover-another-bob-dylan-song-before-it-was-ultimately-rejected/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"The Seeger tune became one of The Byrds' biggest hits.","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilket band hed oprindeligt «The Pendletones», før pladeselskabet ændrede navnet i 1961?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beach_Boys","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Love gave the fledgling band its name: The Pendletones, a pun on Pendleton, a brand of woolen shirt popular among local surfers at the time.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.npr.org/2016/09/27/495638858/the-1961-fishing-trip-that-launched-the-beach-boys","d":"npr.org","q":"He then approached a tiny label called Candix, who thought the name the group was using, The Pendletones after the plaid Pendleton shirts surfers favored, was too obscure","ok":true}]},"mus60|Hvilken 1961-sang af The Tokens bygger på den sydafrikanske sang «Mbube» fra 1939?":{"pool":"mus60","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lion_Sleeps_Tonight","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In 1961, the Tokens adapted the melody and added English lyrics to create The Lion Sleeps Tonight, lending the song the name by which it is best known today.","ok":true},{"u":"https://americansongwriter.com/this-no-1-hit-and-iconic-disney-song-has-a-heartbreaking-backstory/","d":"americansongwriter.com","q":"South African singer/songwriter Solomon Linda and his group, the Original Evening Birds, recorded Mbube in 1939.","ok":true}]},"mus70|Hvem skrev og sang «American Pie», der udkom i 1971?":{"pool":"mus70","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Pie_(song)","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"«American Pie» is a song by the American singer and songwriter Don McLean. It was a commercial success and cultural touchstone","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.loudersound.com/features/the-story-behind-american-pie-by-don-mclean","d":"loudersound.com","q":"I was conscious of the fact that I was trying to create a rock 'n' roll dream sequence. McLean told me in 1997 of his concept for American Pie, but it was way more than r","ok":true}]},"mus70|Hvem sang «Killing Me Softly with His Song» i 1973?":{"pool":"mus70","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-17","daily":true,"sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killing_Me_Softly_with_His_Song","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In 1973, it became a number-one hit in the United States, Australia, and Canada for Roberta Flack","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.udiscovermusic.com/artists/roberta-flack/","d":"udiscovermusic.com","q":"The 1970s: Flack became the first artist 