ackground negotiation and discussion and getting ev","ok":true}],"daily":true},"lang|Hvilket sprog stammer «kangaroo» fra?":{"pool":"lang","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The word kangaroo derives from the Guugu Yimithirr word gangurru, referring to eastern grey kangaroos.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kangaroo","d":"en.wiktionary.org","q":"Borrowed from Guugu Yimidhirr gangurru (“eastern grey kangaroo”).","ok":true}],"daily":true},"lang|Hvilket sprog stammer «ukulele» fra?":{"pool":"lang","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukulele","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"In the Hawaiian language the word ukulele roughly translates as 'jumping flea'","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ukulele","d":"en.wiktionary.org","q":"Borrowed from Hawaiian ʻukulele, from ʻuku (“flea”) + lele (“jump, jumping”).","ok":true}],"daily":true},"lang|Hvilket sprog stammer «wiki» fra?":{"pool":"lang","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiki","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"wiki being a Hawaiian word meaning 'quick'","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wiki","d":"en.wiktionary.org","q":"Abbreviated from WikiWikiWeb, from Hawaiian wikiwiki (“quick”) + English web.","ok":true}],"daily":true},"lang|Hvilket sprog stammer «barbecue» fra?":{"pool":"lang","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbecue","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"The English word barbecue and its cognates in other languages come from the Spanish word barbacoa, which has its origin in a Taíno word.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue","d":"en.wiktionary.org","q":"Borrowed from Spanish barbacoa, from Taíno barbakoa (“framework of sticks”)","ok":true}],"daily":true},"lang|Hvilket sprog stammer «guacamole» fra?":{"pool":"lang","status":"bekræftet","d