nowned for their amazing regenerative capabilities","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ambystoma_mexicanum/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"They possess feathery external gills and finned tails for swimming","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ambystoma_mexicanum/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"neotenic aquatic salamanders, meaning they retain certain larval characteristics in the adult, reproductive state","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ambystoma_mexicanum/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"found in Lakes Chalco and Xochimilco of the Valley of Mexico near Mexico City, Mexico","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Ambystoma_mexicanum/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"Axolotls are paedomorphic or neotenic aquatic salamanders","ok":true}],"daily":true},"who|Koalaen":{"pool":"who","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"weighing only 19.2 g (0.68 oz) on average","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Phascolarctos_cinereus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"sleep up to 18 hours a day","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Phascolarctos_cinereus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"the bulk of their diet comes from only a few eucalypt species","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Phascolarctos_cinereus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"a pouch that opens to the rear and extends upward and forward","ok":true},{"u":"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Phascolarctos_cinereus/","d":"animaldiversity.org","q":"The koalas live in eastern Australia","ok":true}],"daily":true},"dx|{\"a\":\"Kappadokien, Tyrkiet\",\"c\":[\"Området ligger i Centralanatolien i Tyrkiet og er kendt for 'fairy chimneys' – høje, spidsede klippeformationer.\",\"~Området er på UNESCOs verdensarvsliste.\",\"Mange huse og kirker er hugget direkte ud i den bløde vulkanske klippe.\",\"I området findes underjordiske byer, fx Kaymakli og Derinkuyu, hvor folk søgte tilflugt.\",\"~Her er varmluftballoner ved solopgang et berømt syn.\",\"Landskabet skyldes erosion af vulkanske aflejringer fra bl.a. Mount Erciyes.\"],\"e\":\"Snydesporene (UNESCO-status og varmluftballoner) er sande, men vildledende, fordi de gælder for mange steder. Det afgørende er Centralanatolien, fairy chimneys, klippehuse og de underjordiske byer.\"}":{"pool":"dx","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cappadocia","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Cappadocia is a historical region in Central Anatolia region, Turkey.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Cappadocia","d":"en.wikivoyage.org","q":"Between 9 and 3 million years ago, eruptions of Mount Erciyes and Mount Hasan covered the area in fine ash particles, which welded together and packed down into a deep la","ok":true}],"daily":true},"dx|{\"a\":\"Galápagosøerne, Ecuador\",\"c\":[\"Øerne ligger i Stillehavet, ca. 1.000 km vest for Ecuador.\",\"~Øerne tilhører Ecuador.\",\"Øerne er berømte for endemiske arter som kæmpeskildpadder, havleguaner og Darwinfinker.\",\"Charles Darwin besøgte øerne i 1830'erne og blev inspireret til sin evolutionsteori.\",\"~Øerne ligger på ækvator.\",\"~Øerne er på UNESCOs verdensarvsliste.\"],\"e\":\"Snydesporene (Ecuador, ækvator, UNESCO) er sande, men vildledende, fordi de gælder for mange steder. Det afgørende er Stillehavet/afstanden, de endemiske arter og Darwin.\"}":{"pool":"dx","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galápagos_Islands","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"are an archipelago of volcanic islands in the Eastern Pacific, located around the equator, 485 nautical miles (898 km; 558 mi) west of the mainland of South America.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Galápagos_Islands","d":"en.wikivoyage.org","q":"in the eastern Pacific Ocean. The islands are quite remote and isolated, lying some 1000 km (620 miles) west of the South American continent, and the archipelago is bisec","ok":true}],"daily":true},"dx|{\"a\":\"Victoria Falls, Zambia/Zimbabwe\",\"c\":[\"Vandfaldet ligger på grænsen mellem Zambia og Zimbabwe på Zambezi-floden.\",\"Det er et af verdens største vandfald med en bredde på 1.708 meter.\",\"Det lokale navn er 'Mosi-oa-Tunya', som betyder 'torden, der ryger'.\",\"~Vandfaldet er på UNESCOs verdensarvsliste.\",\"Vandfaldet styrtede ned i en kløft i et basaltplateau.\",\"~David Livingstone opkaldte det efter dronning Victoria i 1855.\"],\"e\":\"Snydesporene (UNESCO-status og Livingstone) er sande, men vildledende. Det afgørende er grænsen Zambia/Zimbabwe, bredden, det lokale navn og basaltkløften.\"}":{"pool":"dx","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_Falls","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"is a waterfall on the Zambezi River, located on the border between Zambia and Zimbabwe.","ok":true},{"u":"https://www.zambiatourism.com/destinations/waterfalls/victoria-falls/","d":"zambiatourism.com","q":"The wide basalt cliff over which the Falls thunder transforms the Zambezi from a placid river into a ferocious torrent cutting through a series of dramatic gorges.","ok":true}],"daily":true},"kwho|{\"a\":\"Zebra\",\"age\":4,\"c\":[\"Jeg bor i Afrika.\",\"Jeg er et hestedyr med sort og hvid stribet pels.\",\"Hver zebras striber er unikke, ligesom fingeraftryk.\",\"Jeg spiser græs.\",\"Jeg kan løbe hurtigt og lever i flokke.\"]}":{"pool":"kwho","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zebra","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Zebras are African equines with distinctive black-and-white striped coats.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zebra","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Zebra stripes come in different patterns, unique to each individual.","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/zebra","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"zebras are equids members of the horse family","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/zebra","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"zebra stripes are unique to each individual","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/zebra","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"zebras are herbivores and feed mostly by grazing on grasses","ok":true}],"daily":true},"kwho|{\"a\":\"Koala\",\"age\":6,\"c\":[\"Jeg er et pungdyr, der bor i Australien.\",\"Jeg spiser næsten kun blade fra eukalyptustræer.\",\"Jeg sover op til 20 timer om dagen.\",\"Min unge kaldes en joey og bor i min pung.\",\"Jeg ligner en lille bjørn, men er ikke en bjørn.\"]}":{"pool":"kwho","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources":[{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"Koalas are largely sedentary and sleep up to twenty hours a day.","ok":true},{"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","d":"wikipedia.org","q":"the leaves of these trees make up most of their diet","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/koala","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"koalas are native to southeastern and eastern australia living in forests of eucalypt trees","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/koala","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"they need to sleep a lot to give them time to digest their food","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/koala","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"female marsupials have a pouch in which they carry their baby called a joey","ok":true},{"u":"https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/koala","d":"animals.sandiegozoo.org","q":"koalas are not bears they are members of a group of pouched mammals called marsupials","ok":true}],"daily":true},"kwho|{\"a\":\"Hvalross\",\"age\":11,\"c\":[\"Jeg lever i Arktis, nær Nordpolen.\",\"Jeg har to lange stødtænder.\",\"Jeg har mange følsomme skægvædder.\",\"Jeg spiser mest muslinger fra havbunden.\",\"Jeg er et stort pattedyr med et tykt fedtlag.\"]}":{"pool":"kwho","status":"bekræftet","date":"2026-11-20","sources"